msgid ""
"where the flow is driven in; where it leaves, at the reference pressure; "
"walls. The part is the fluid volume, and every surface that is neither an "
"inlet nor an outlet is a wall"
msgstr "流动从哪里被驱入；它从哪里离开，离开处取参考压力；壁面。零件就是流体体积，而既不是入口也不是出口的每一个表面都是壁面"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:699
msgid ""
"An analysis refuses a key it does not read: ``outlet:`` on a stress "
"analysis, or ``fix:`` on a heat one, would read as a boundary condition and "
"not be one."
msgstr "分析会拒绝它不读取的键：应力分析上的 ``outlet:`` ，或者传热分析上的 ``fix:`` ，看起来像边界条件而其实不是。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:702
msgid ""
"A ``load`` value is a **force**. It may be written as a number and a unit — "
"``n``, ``nm``, ``mn``, ``kn`` or ``newton`` for force, ``mg``, ``g``, "
"``kg``, ``ton``, ``tonne``, ``lb`` or ``pound`` for mass — matched case-"
"insensitively, with or without a space in front of it and with or without a "
"plural ``s``. A bare number is a **mass in kilograms**, which is what \"the "
"shelf carries 5\" means. A mass is weighed into a force at 9.8 N/kg, so what"
" is stored and handed to the solver is always newtons."
msgstr ""
"``load`` 的值是一个 **力**。它可以写成数字加单位 — 力的单位有 ``n``、``nm``、``mn``、``kn`` 或 "
"``newton``，质量的单位有 ``mg``、``g``、``kg``、``ton``、``tonne``、``lb`` 或 ``pound`` —"
" 匹配时不区分大小写，单位前可以有空格也可以没有，可以带复数 ``s`` 也可以不带。只写一个数字表示 "
"**以千克为单位的质量**，这也正是“这块搁板承载 5”的含义。质量按 9.8 N/kg 换算成力，因此存储下来并交给求解器的始终是牛顿。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:708
msgid ""
"A force so written is a magnitude, and the implementation applies it the way"
" it always has — CalculiX straight down, along -Z, which is where a weight "
"goes. A ``load`` may also be **three** of them, ``[x, y, z]`` in the part's "
"own frame: a force *with a direction*, which is what a simulation measures "
"acting on a part (see :ref:`sim-loads`). And an ``fea:`` scenario takes one "
"key that names no interface, ``gravity:``, the acceleration of free fall the"
" part is analysed in, in m/s² and the part's own frame — for a part a "
"simulation found upside down, or accelerating, whose weight is then its mass"
" times ``g - a``. Without it the implementation weighs the part under its "
"own gravity::"
msgstr ""
"这样写出的力是一个大小，而实现方会按它一向的方式施加它 — CalculiX 是竖直向下，沿 -Z 方向，也就是重量所指的方向。``load`` "
"也可以是 **三个** 数，在零件自身坐标系中的 ``[x, y, z]`` ：一个 *带方向的* 力，这正是仿真所测得的作用在零件上的量（参见 "
":ref:`sim-loads` ）。而 ``fea:`` 场景还接受一个不指名任何接口的键，``gravity:`` "
"，即分析该零件时所处的自由落体加速度，单位 m/s²，在零件自身坐标系中 — 用于仿真发现它上下颠倒、或者正在加速的零件，此时它的重量是它的质量乘以 "
"``g - a``。不写它时，实现方按它自身的重力来计算零件的重量::"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:725
msgid ""
"A name under an interface is one of its instances, or one of their "
"**ports**: a gear draws each tooth as a port of one instance, so a tooth is "
"loaded by its port's name. That is a whole example, in "
"``examples/feature_simulate_fea``: the gear in a robot arm's knee, under "
"what the worm holds it with at the end of a simulation of the arm -- the "
"scenario the ``/pc:sim-assembly-fea`` skill adds, named after the simulation"
" it came from."
msgstr ""
"接口下面的某个名称，指的是它的某个实例，或者这些实例的某个 "
"**端口**：齿轮会把每一个齿都画成某个实例的一个端口，所以一个齿是按它端口的名称来加载的。这就是一个完整的例子，在 "
"``examples/feature_simulate_fea`` 中：机器人手臂膝关节里的那个齿轮，承受着手臂仿真结束时蜗轮把它固定住所用的力 -- "
"也就是 ``/pc:sim-assembly-fea`` 技能添加的那个场景，以它所来自的那个仿真命名。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:731
msgid ""
"Both have to be *read* by the implementation, and one that does not would "
"answer as if they had not been written. So an implementation says which it "
"reads (``reads:`` on its file type, see :ref:`cae-section`), and an analysis"
" that states one is refused by an implementation that does not, naming it "
"and what to do about it. ``//pub/feature/cae/calculix:fea`` reads both. A "
"``temperature`` is in **degrees Celsius**, and ``300 K`` or ``100 F`` are "
"converted; a ``heat`` is a **power**, in watts (``mW`` and ``kW`` are "
"understood), put in through the whole of the port's surface; a "
"``convection`` is a **film coefficient** in W/(m²·K)."
msgstr ""
"这两者都必须被实现方真正 *读取*，而不读取它们的实现方给出的答案就跟它们没被写过一样。所以实现方会说明它读取哪些（它的文件类型上的 "
"``reads:`` ，参见 :ref:`cae-section` "
"），而一个写明了某个条件的分析会被不读取该条件的实现方拒绝，并指出是哪一个以及该怎么办。``//pub/feature/cae/calculix:fea``"
" 两者都读取。``temperature`` 的单位是 **摄氏度**，而 ``300 K`` 或 ``100 F`` 会被换算；``heat`` "
"是一个 **功率**，单位为瓦（ ``mW`` 和 ``kW`` 也能看懂），它是通过端口的整个表面输入的；``convection`` 是一个 "
"**表面换热系数**，单位 W/(m²·K)。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:739
msgid ""
"**Where a condition lands** is the surface its port stands for. A port is a "
"coordinate frame; when its interface draws it with a sketch — ``sketch:`` on"
" the port, often a ``basic`` ``circle:`` — the sketch, placed by the port's "
"frame with Z out of the surface, is that surface. PartCAD imprints every "
"port's sketch on the part before the implementation runs and hands it the "
"faces each port covers, and their area is what a force or a power is spread "
"over: an inlet drawn as the bore's circle is exactly the bore. A port with "
"no sketch covers the face it lies on, when it lies on one."
msgstr ""
"**条件落在哪里**，取决于它的端口所代表的那个表面。端口是一个坐标系；当它的接口用草图把它画出来时 — 端口上的 ``sketch:`` ，常常是一个"
" ``basic`` 的 ``circle:`` — 那个按端口坐标系（Z 轴指向表面外侧）放置的草图就是那个表面。PartCAD "
"会在实现方运行之前把每个端口的草图印到零件上，并把每个端口所覆盖的那些面交给它，而这些面的面积就是力或功率被分摊到的面积：画成孔的那个圆的入口，正好就是那个孔。没有草图的端口覆盖它所在的那个面，前提是它确实落在某个面上。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:746
msgid ""
"A sketch that lies on no surface — a gear tooth's cross-section at its pitch"
" circle, a hole's outline drawn over the hole — still says where its port "
"is, and the condition is applied to the surface around it instead: "
"everything within ``port_radius`` of the port (a fraction of the part's "
"largest dimension, 5 % unless the implementation says otherwise — the same "
"neighbourhood an implementation that loads mesh nodes near a port takes). "
"PartCAD divides a plane, a cylinder, a cone, a sphere or a torus where that "
"neighbourhood ends, and takes a freeform face that comes that near whole, "
"because a curve drawn on one is what a mesher fails on. Either way the "
"analysis warns, naming the port and the area it loaded: the port's frame is "
"still worth correcting."
msgstr ""
"没有落在任何表面上的草图 — 比如齿轮齿在其节圆处的横截面、画在孔上方的孔轮廓 — 仍然说明它的端口在哪里，而条件会改为施加在它周围的表面上：也就是端口"
" ``port_radius`` 以内的所有部分（它是零件最大尺寸的一个比例，除实现方另有说明外为 5 "
"%，与那些会加载端口附近网格节点的实现方所取的邻域相同）。PartCAD "
"会在那个邻域的边界处切分平面、圆柱面、圆锥面、球面或圆环面，而对于靠得那么近的自由曲面则整个取用，因为画在自由曲面上的曲线正是网格器会失败的地方。无论哪种情况，分析都会给出警告，并指出端口以及它所加载的面积：端口的坐标系仍然值得去修正。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:754
msgid ""
"The model each scenario produces is written to "
"``<part>.<analysis>.<scenario>.<extension>`` (``bracket.fea.loaded.glb``, "
"with a ``/`` in the name written ``_``) and saved as it stands. Two "
"scenarios of one section whose models would be one file -- ``arm/held`` and "
"``arm_held``, or ``Loaded`` and ``loaded``, which are one file wherever a "
"filesystem ignores case -- are refused rather than left to overwrite each "
"other's. Which format the model is — 3D or 2D — is the implementation's "
"choice, and PartCAD does not convert it. The **findings** are the other half"
" of the answer: a JSON array of what the analysis has to say about the part,"
" printed as a table under the scenario it is of, or with ``--json`` as one "
"array of every scenario's findings, each carrying the ``scenario`` it is of."
" ``pc cae`` exits non-zero when there is at least one, or when a scenario "
"did not run -- each says why in the log, and the others are run all the same"
" -- so it can be used as a gate."
msgstr ""
"每个场景所产生的模型会写入 ``<part>.<analysis>.<scenario>.<extension>`` （ "
"``bracket.fea.loaded.glb`` ，名称中的 ``/`` 写作 ``_`` "
"），并按原样保存。同一小节中两个场景的模型如果会落到同一个文件上 -- 比如 ``arm/held`` 和 ``arm_held``，或者 "
"``Loaded`` 和 ``loaded`` （在忽略大小写的文件系统上它们是同一个文件）-- 会被拒绝，而不是放任它们互相覆盖。模型是什么格式 — "
"3D 还是 2D — 由实现方决定，PartCAD 不会对它进行转换。**各项发现** 是答案的另一半：一个 JSON "
"数组，内容是该分析对这个零件有什么要说的，按它所属的场景以表格形式打印出来，或者加上 ``--json`` "
"时打印为一个汇总所有场景发现的数组，其中每一条都带着它所属的 ``scenario``。只要至少有一条发现，或者有某个场景没能运行 -- "
"每一个都会在日志里说明原因，而其余场景照样会运行 -- ``pc cae`` 就会以非零状态退出，因此它可以用作一道关卡。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:765
msgid ""
"Who runs the analysis is ``<package>:<file type>``. It defaults to the "
":doc:`user configuration </maintenance/automation>` option named after the "
"analysis — ``caeFeaImplementation`` (``//pub/feature/cae/calculix:fea``), "
"``caeDynamicImplementation`` (``//pub/feature/cae/elmer:dynamic``), "
"``caeThermalImplementation`` (``//pub/feature/cae/elmer:thermal``) and "
"``caeCfdImplementation`` (``//pub/feature/cae/openfoam:cfd``) — a scenario's"
" own ``implementation:`` outranks that, and ``-i``/``--implementation`` "
"outranks both for one run. PartCAD ships no solver: an implementation is a "
"package like any other, declared in a ``cae:`` section exactly as an export "
"or a render implementation is declared in its own (see :ref:`output-files`),"
" and installed as a dependency."
msgstr ""
"由谁来运行分析由 ``<package>:<file type>`` 指定。它默认取 :doc:`用户配置 "
"</maintenance/automation>` 中以该分析命名的那个选项 — ``caeFeaImplementation`` （ "
"``//pub/feature/cae/calculix:fea`` ）、``caeDynamicImplementation`` （ "
"``//pub/feature/cae/elmer:dynamic`` ）、``caeThermalImplementation`` （ "
"``//pub/feature/cae/elmer:thermal`` ）和 ``caeCfdImplementation`` （ "
"``//pub/feature/cae/openfoam:cfd`` ） — 场景自己的 ``implementation:`` 优先于它，而 "
"``-i``/``--implementation`` 则为单次运行优先于两者。PartCAD 不提供任何求解器：实现方就是一个和其他包一样的包，在 "
"``cae:`` 小节中声明，方式与导出或渲染的实现在各自小节中的声明完全相同（参见 :ref:`output-files` ），并作为依赖安装。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:774
msgid ""
"An analysis that produces no answer is reported the same way by ``pc cae`` "
"and by ``pc test``: which implementation was asked, what it said, and which "
"platform it did not work on. The remedies differ — install a solver, use "
"another machine, fix the part — and only the implementation's own sentence "
"says which, so it is relayed as it stands rather than classified. The "
"command and the check say it identically on purpose: a user who ran one of "
"them and then the other must not be told two different things about the same"
" machine."
msgstr ""
"对于给不出答案的分析， ``pc cae`` 和 ``pc test`` "
"的报告方式完全一致：询问的是哪个实现、它说了什么、以及它在哪个平台上无法工作。补救办法各不相同——安装求解器、换一台机器、修正零件——而只有实现方自己给出的那句话才能说明该用哪一种，因此这句话会被原样转述，而不会被归类。命令和检查说法完全一致是有意为之：先后运行过这两者的用户，不应该就同一台机器得到两种不同的说法。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:780
msgid ""
"``pc test`` runs the same analyses. Its ``fea``, ``dynamic``, ``thermal`` "
"and ``cfd`` tests apply to a part that declares the matching section — and "
"to nothing else, so a package of bolts pays nothing for them — and run every"
" scenario of it, failing the part on any of them and naming which. **One "
"thing passes: every scenario ran and reported no findings.** A malformed "
"section fails; a plugin that cannot be resolved fails (the package is not a "
"dependency, did not load, or declares no such file type — the configuration "
"is wrong wherever the package is opened); a plugin that resolves and cannot "
"run fails too, whether what is missing is the solver, the mesher, or a "
"sandbox that will not build. That last one is not a skip on purpose: a part "
"declaring ``fea:`` has asked a question, and a plugin that answered nothing "
"has failed. So declaring ``fea:`` in a shared package does make ``pc test`` "
"fail for everyone who has not installed what the implementation needs — that"
" is what declaring it means, and a package unwilling to ask that of its "
"readers should not declare the section. It is the one verdict ``pc test`` "
"does not remember — installing a solver changes nothing a cache key is built"
" from, so a remembered one would go on failing a part that now analyses "
"perfectly well."
msgstr ""
"``pc test`` 运行的是同样的分析。它的 ``fea``、``dynamic``、``thermal`` 和 ``cfd`` "
"测试只适用于声明了相应小节的零件 — 除此之外一概不适用，因此一个装满螺栓的包不会为它们付出任何代价 — "
"并且会运行它的每一个场景，任何一个场景不通过都会让该零件失败，并指出是哪一个。**只有一种情况算通过：每一个场景都运行了，并且没有报告任何发现。** "
"格式有误的小节算失败；无法解析的插件算失败（该包不是依赖、没能加载，或者没有声明这种文件类型 — "
"无论在哪里打开这个包，配置都是错的）；能够解析却无法运行的插件同样算失败，无论缺的是求解器、网格器，还是一个构建不起来的沙箱。最后这一种有意不算跳过：声明了"
" ``fea:`` 的零件已经提出了一个问题，而什么也没回答的插件就是失败了。因此，在共享的包中声明 ``fea:`` "
"确实会让每一个没有安装该实现所需内容的人 ``pc test`` 失败 — 这正是声明它的含义，而不愿对读者提出这种要求的包就不应该声明这个小节。它也是"
" ``pc test`` 唯一不会记住的判定结果 — "
"安装求解器并不会改变任何参与缓存键计算的内容，于是一个被记住的失败结果会让一个如今完全能分析通过的零件继续失败下去。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:794
msgid ""
"**A machine with no container runtime is the one excuse.** An implementation"
" naming a ``container:`` or a ``dockerImage`` (see :doc:`/config_package`) "
"is saying that a container is how what pip cannot install arrives; where "
"there is no container runtime to run it in, nothing was ever asked, and the "
"check skips with a ``WARNING`` carrying the whole report. It still declares "
"the requirements that let it run in a ``conda`` or ``venv`` sandbox, so a "
"host with the non-Python pieces installed natively runs it there and a "
"failure there is a failure. An implementation that names no image gets no "
"excuse at all, and a container runtime that *is* here removes the excuse for"
" one that does — an image that cannot be pulled or is missing the solver is "
"something somebody can fix. A Docker daemon running Windows containers is "
"not one of these runtimes: every image PartCAD uses is a Linux image."
msgstr ""
"**唯一的例外是没有容器运行时的机器。** 指名了 ``container:`` 或 ``dockerImage`` 的实现（参见 "
":doc:`/config_package` ）等于在说：pip "
"装不上的那些东西是通过容器送达的；而在没有容器运行时可供运行它的地方，根本就没有提出过任何问题，于是该检查会跳过，并给出一条带有完整报告的 "
"``WARNING``。它仍然会声明那些让它能在 ``conda`` 或 ``venv`` 沙箱中运行的依赖要求，因此在已原生安装了非 Python "
"组件的主机上，它会在那里运行，而在那里失败就是失败。完全没有指名镜像的实现得不到任何例外；而一旦机器上 *确实* "
"有容器运行时，指名了镜像的实现也就失去了这项例外 — 拉不下来的镜像或缺少求解器的镜像，是有人可以修好的问题。运行 Windows 容器的 Docker"
" 守护进程不属于这里所说的运行时：PartCAD 使用的每一个镜像都是 Linux 镜像。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:806
msgid "``pc cam``"
msgstr "``pc cam``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:807
msgid ""
"Produce the route files of the objects that declare one: the program a "
"machine cuts them with. It takes the object's own outline, offsets it by the"
" radius of the cutter, and cuts it at a series of depths -- a 2.5D route, "
"which is what a CNC router does to sheet goods and what a mill does to a "
"plate::"
msgstr ""
"为声明了加工路径的对象生成路径文件：也就是机器切削它们所用的程序。它取对象自身的轮廓，按刀具半径做偏置，然后在一系列深度上逐层切削——这是一条 2.5D"
" 的加工路径，正是 CNC 雕刻机加工板材、铣床加工平板时所做的事： ::"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:818
msgid ""
"Unlike ``pc cae``, this is a **package-level** command. An analysis is asked"
" of one part; a route is what a package's cut list is made of, so with "
"nothing named ``pc cam`` produces one for every sketch and part of the "
"package that says how it is made and passes over every object that does not,"
" silently. Most objects are never cut, and a package where three parts of "
"forty are is the ordinary case rather than thirty-seven warnings. Naming an "
"object that declares nothing *is* an error: naming one is asking about it, "
"and coming back with nothing would look exactly like a route that went "
"somewhere the user did not notice. An assembly and a scene are not routed at"
" all -- an assembly is put together rather than cut, and a scene is an "
"arrangement of things that were each cut on their own."
msgstr ""
"与 ``pc cae`` 不同，这是一条 **包级别** 的命令。分析是针对单个零件提出的；而加工路径构成的是一个包的切削清单，因此在不指名任何对象时，"
" ``pc cam`` "
"会为包中每一个说明了自己如何制造的草图和零件各生成一条路径，并静默跳过所有没有说明的对象。大多数对象根本不会被切削，一个包中四十个零件里只有三个要切削才是常态，而不是三十七条警告。但指名一个什么也没声明的对象"
" *就是* "
"错误：指名它就是在询问它，而什么也不返回，看起来会和一条写到了用户没注意到的地方的路径一模一样。装配体和场景完全不生成路径——装配体是拼装起来的而不是切削出来的，而场景是一组各自单独切削出来的东西的布置。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:827
msgid ""
"The object says what is cut out of it, and how, in the ``manufacturing:`` "
"section that already says how it is made -- beside the machine it belongs "
"to::"
msgstr ""
"对象在那个本就说明了它如何制造的 ``manufacturing:`` 小节中，说明从它身上切出什么、以及怎么切——就写在它所属的机器旁边： ::"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:848
msgid ""
"A key written directly under ``manufacturing:`` is shared by every machine "
"the part names; one written inside a machine's own subsection is that "
"machine's and outranks it. A part may name several -- ``cnc:``, ``laser:``, "
"``drill:`` -- and they are **alternatives**, ways it could be made rather "
"than stages it goes through, so ``--machine`` picks which to write for and "
"the programs land beside each other as ``panel.laser.nc`` and "
"``panel.cnc.nc``. A part that really is machined in stages is a chain of "
"parts, each naming the previous one as its ``source``."
msgstr ""
"直接写在 ``manufacturing:`` "
"之下的键，由该零件所指定的每一台机器共用；写在某台机器自己的子小节中的键则属于那台机器，并且优先级更高。一个零件可以指定好几台机器—— ``cnc:``"
" 、 ``laser:`` 、 ``drill:`` ——它们是 **互为替代的方案** "
"，是它可以被制造出来的几种方式，而不是它依次要经过的几道工序，因此用 ``--machine`` 选择为哪一台生成程序，而生成的程序会并排落在一起，比如"
" ``panel.laser.nc`` 和 ``panel.cnc.nc`` "
"。真正要分多道工序加工的零件，应当写成一串零件，每一个都把前一个指定为自己的 ``source`` 。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:857
msgid ""
"A *sketch* has one of these sections too, with no ``method:`` in it: a "
"drawing is not made from anything, it is a path a machine follows."
msgstr "*草图* 也有这样一个小节，只是其中没有 ``method:`` ：图样不是由任何东西制成的，它就是一条机器要走的路径。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:860
msgid ""
"``operation:`` says which side of the outline the tool runs on. ``profile`` "
"goes around the outside of the material and around the inside of every hole,"
" so the object survives at its nominal size -- and cuts the holes first, "
"because a profile cut ends by separating the part from its stock and a hole "
"cut after that is cut in something that is no longer held. ``pocket`` clears"
" what is inside the outline, ring by ring, innermost first so that the wall "
"is cut last by a tool engaged on one side rather than buried in a slot; an "
"island in the middle of one is refused rather than cut through. ``engrave`` "
"follows the outline itself, offset by nothing, which is what a V-bit or a "
"drag knife wants."
msgstr ""
"``operation:`` 说明刀具沿轮廓的哪一侧走。 ``profile`` "
"沿材料的外侧以及每个孔的内侧走刀，因此对象能以其名义尺寸保留下来——并且会先切孔，因为轮廓切削的最后一刀会把零件与原材料分离，而在那之后再去切孔，切的就是一块已经不再被夹持的东西了。"
" ``pocket`` "
"清除轮廓以内的材料，一圈一圈地来，从最内圈开始，这样壁面是最后被切的，刀具只有一侧参与切削，而不是整个埋在槽里；型腔中间的凸岛会被拒绝，而不是被直接切掉。"
" ``engrave`` 则沿轮廓本身走刀，不做任何偏置，这正是 V 型刀或拖刀所需要的。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:868
msgid ""
"A length may be written as a number and a unit -- ``mm``, ``cm``, ``m``, "
"``um``, ``in``, ``inch``, ``\"``, ``ft``, ``mil`` or ``thou`` -- matched "
"case-insensitively, with or without a space in front of it and with or "
"without a plural. A bare number is **millimetres**. A feed may name the "
"length, the time, or both: ``2400``, ``2400 mm/min``, ``40 mm/s``, ``60 "
"in/min``; a bare number is millimetres per minute. A spindle speed is rpm, "
"with or without the word. What the *file* is written in is a separate "
"question and the ``units:`` parameter of the file type: a part 18 mm thick "
"is cut 18 mm deep whether the program says ``G21`` or ``G20``."
msgstr ""
"长度可以写成数字加单位—— ``mm`` 、 ``cm`` 、 ``m`` 、 ``um`` 、 ``in`` 、 ``inch`` 、 ``\"`` "
"、 ``ft`` 、 ``mil`` 或 ``thou`` ——匹配时不区分大小写，单位前可以有空格也可以没有，可以带复数也可以不带。只写一个数字表示 "
"**毫米** 。进给量可以只写长度、只写时间，或者两者都写： ``2400`` 、 ``2400 mm/min`` 、 ``40 mm/s`` 、 "
"``60 in/min`` ；只写一个数字表示毫米每分钟。主轴转速以 rpm 为单位，写不写这个词都可以。 *文件* "
"本身用什么单位书写是另一个问题，由该文件类型的 ``units:`` 参数决定：一个 18 mm 厚的零件，无论程序里写的是 ``G21`` 还是 "
"``G20`` ，切深都是 18 mm。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:876
msgid ""
"``safe_z:`` is a **clearance above the top of the object** rather than an "
"absolute height, so it means the same thing wherever the object sits in Z."
msgstr ""
"``safe_z:`` 是 **相对于对象顶面的安全高度** ，而不是一个绝对高度，因此无论对象在 Z 方向上处于什么位置，它的含义都相同。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:879
msgid ""
"``depth:`` is the one key with a conditional default. An object that does "
"not say is cut **through**, from the top of its bounding box to the bottom. "
"A sketch has no thickness to be cut through, so a sketch that does not say "
"how deep to cut is refused. ``diameter:`` has no default at all and must not"
" get one: every other parameter has a defensible default, and the diameter "
"of the cutter is the one number that cannot be guessed from the part -- a "
"route produced against a diameter nobody chose is wrong by exactly the "
"amount nobody noticed."
msgstr ""
"``depth:`` 是唯一一个带条件默认值的键。没有说明的对象会被 **切穿** "
"，从其包围盒的顶面一直切到底面。草图没有可供切穿的厚度，因此没有说明切多深的草图会被拒绝。 ``diameter:`` "
"则完全没有默认值，而且绝不能给它加一个：其他每一个参数都有站得住脚的默认值，而刀具直径是唯一一个无法从零件推断出来的数字——按一个没人选过的直径生成的加工路径，其错误量恰恰就是没人注意到的那个量。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:886
msgid ""
"Every key of that section is also a parameter of the ``cam:`` file type that"
" produces the route, which is what makes it three layers of one namespace: "
"``//builtin/cam`` underneath, then the package's own ``cam:`` section, then "
"the object's ``manufacturing:``. So a package cutting twenty parts from one "
"sheet sets the cutter once and the one part that needs a smaller one says so"
" for itself. The conversion above happens at every layer -- a ``mm/min`` "
"written by the package is understood as surely as one written on the object."
msgstr ""
"该小节的每一个键同时也是生成加工路径的 ``cam:`` 文件类型的参数，这使它成了同一个命名空间上的三层结构：最底下是 "
"``//builtin/cam`` ，然后是包自己的 ``cam:`` 小节，再然后是对象的 ``manufacturing:`` "
"。于是，一个要从同一张板材上切出二十个零件的包只需设置一次刀具，而唯一需要更小刀具的那个零件自己说明即可。上面所说的换算在每一层都会发生——包里写的 "
"``mm/min`` 和写在对象上的一样能被正确理解。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:892
msgid ""
"The route is written to ``<object>.<extension>`` -- ``panel.nc`` -- beside "
"the package, or wherever ``-O`` says. ``--json`` prints what was produced as"
" the array it is: the file, the implementation that wrote it, and whatever "
"that implementation counted about the route. ``pc cam`` exits non-zero if "
"any object it was asked about produced no route, and reports every one of "
"them rather than stopping at the first: a route is a file, and an object "
"whose section is wrong must not cost the other nineteen theirs."
msgstr ""
"加工路径会写入 ``<object>.<extension>`` ——比如 ``panel.nc`` ——放在包旁边，或者放在 ``-O`` "
"所指定的位置。 ``--json`` "
"会把生成的结果按其本来的数组形式打印出来：文件、写出它的实现，以及该实现对这条路径所统计的各项数据。只要被询问的对象中有任何一个没有生成出路径， "
"``pc cam`` "
"就会以非零状态退出，并且会把它们全部报告出来，而不是在第一个失败处停下：加工路径就是文件，而一个小节写错了的对象，不该让另外十九个对象失去它们的文件。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:898
msgid ""
"Who produces it is ``<package>:<file type>``. Unlike an analysis, PartCAD "
"**ships one** -- a route is arithmetic on the object's own outline rather "
"than somebody else's program with a release cycle of its own, which is the "
"test ``export:`` and ``render:`` already pass -- so ``camImplementation`` "
"defaults to ``//builtin/cam:gcode`` and nothing has to be installed. A "
"controller that wants a dialect of its own is a package declaring a file "
"type in its own ``cam:`` section exactly as an export or a render "
"implementation is declared in its own (see :ref:`output-files`), named by "
"that option, by an ``implementation:`` in the object's own "
"``manufacturing:`` section, or by ``-i`` for one run -- in that order of "
"precedence, narrowest last."
msgstr ""
"由谁来生成它由 ``<package>:<file type>`` 指定。与分析不同，PartCAD **自带了一个** "
"——加工路径是在对象自身轮廓上做的算术，而不是别人那套有着自己发布周期的程序，这正是 ``export:`` 和 ``render:`` "
"早已通过的检验——因此 ``camImplementation`` 默认为 ``//builtin/cam:gcode`` "
"，什么都不用安装。需要自有方言的控制器，就是一个在自己的 ``cam:`` "
"小节中声明文件类型的包，方式与导出或渲染的实现在各自小节中的声明完全相同（参见 :ref:`output-files` ），可以由该选项指定、由对象自己"
" ``manufacturing:`` 小节中的 ``implementation:`` 指定，或者由 ``-i`` "
"为单次运行指定——优先级依次递增，最具体的排在最后。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:907
msgid ""
"What the built-in one writes is plain RS-274 with every curve linearized to "
"within ``tolerance:`` of the true curve: an arc word is only an arc while "
"the plane it was written in survives the post-processor, and one tolerance "
"says exactly what the approximation costs where an arc and a tolerance would"
" say less. Nothing in the file is a timestamp, a host name or a version, so "
"the same object and the same parameters produce the same bytes on any "
"machine."
msgstr ""
"内置实现写出的是纯粹的 RS-274，其中每一条曲线都被线性化到与真实曲线相差不超过 ``tolerance:`` "
"：圆弧指令只有在它所在的平面能挺过后处理器时才还是圆弧，而一个公差值恰好说明了这种近似的代价有多大，换成圆弧加公差反而说得更少。文件中没有任何时间戳、主机名或版本号，因此同一个对象、同一组参数，在任何机器上都会产生完全相同的字节。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:913
msgid ""
"``pc test`` runs this as its ``cam`` check, and it is the same code: the "
"check produces the route and passes the object only if one came back. It "
"applies to an object that says how it is made and to nothing else, so a "
"package of bolts pays nothing for it -- the same gate the analysis checks "
"have, and the same cost model. There is one way to pass: a route was "
"written. A malformed section fails, an implementation that cannot be "
"resolved fails, and an implementation that resolved and produced nothing "
"fails -- a tool bigger than the hole it was asked to cut, an outline the "
"offset consumed, a sandbox that will not build. A machine that cannot "
"provision a sandbox at all is the one thing it does not hold against the "
"object: nothing was ever asked there, so it skips, loudly, and does not "
"remember the skip."
msgstr ""
"``pc test`` 把这件事作为它的 ``cam`` "
"检查来运行，而且用的就是同一份代码：该检查会生成加工路径，只有真的生成出来了，对象才算通过。它只适用于说明了自己如何制造的对象，除此之外一概不适用，因此一个装满螺栓的包不会为它付出任何代价"
" -- "
"与各项分析检查相同的门槛，也是相同的代价模型。通过只有一种方式：路径被写了出来。格式有误的小节算失败，无法解析的实现算失败，能够解析却什么也没生成出来的实现同样算失败"
" -- "
"刀具比要切的孔还大、轮廓被偏置吃掉了、沙箱构建不起来。唯一不会算到对象头上的，是机器根本无法准备沙箱这一种情况：那里从来没有提出过任何问题，因此它会跳过，而且会大声地跳过，并且不会记住这次跳过。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:922
msgid ""
"Unlike the analyses, the check does **not** keep what it produced. An "
"analysis writes its model beside the package because the model is the answer"
" somebody asked for; a route produced by a check is a by-product, and one "
"left beside the package would be indistinguishable from the one this command"
" writes -- checked in by accident, or read as current long after the part "
"moved on. So the check routes into a temporary directory and deletes it."
msgstr ""
"与各项分析不同，该检查 **不会** "
"保留它所生成的东西。分析之所以把模型写在包旁边，是因为那个模型正是有人要的答案；而检查生成的加工路径只是副产品，一份留在包旁边的副产品会与这条命令写出的那一份难以区分——可能被意外提交进版本库，也可能在零件早已变化之后仍被当作最新的来读。因此该检查把路径生成到一个临时目录中，随后删除它。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:928
msgid ""
"**The check that used to be called ``cam`` is ``manufacturability`` now.** "
"It asks whether an object *can* be made or bought at all -- whether the "
"geometry suits the method it declares, whether what it is made from is "
"reproducible, whether a supplier could be found -- which is a different "
"question from whether a post-processor can produce a program for it. Both "
"are computer-aided manufacturing, which is why one word answered for both "
"until this command existed."
msgstr ""
"**原先叫做 ``cam`` 的那项检查现在叫 ``manufacturability`` 。** 它问的是一个对象究竟 *能不能* "
"被制造出来或买到——几何形状是否适合它所声明的工艺方法、它所用的材料是否可复现、是否能找到供应商——这与后处理器能否为它生成程序是两个不同的问题。两者都属于计算机辅助制造，这也正是在这条命令出现之前，一个词同时回答了两件事的原因。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:934
msgid ""
"**The outline is a section taken at the bottom of the cut**, and that is the"
" limit worth knowing. For a prismatic object -- a panel, a plate, a gasket, "
"anything cut out of stock of one thickness -- it is the same outline at "
"every depth. For an object whose cross-section changes over the cut there is"
" no single right answer, and the route follows the bottom and says so, as a "
"warning naming how much the two ends differ by: a route produced from an "
"outline the user did not expect is the one failure that looks like a success"
" all the way to the machine. There is also no lead-in, no tab and no ramp --"
" the tool plunges at the start of each contour and the part is free at the "
"end of the last pass."
msgstr ""
"**轮廓取的是切削底面处的那个截面** "
"，而这正是值得了解的限制所在。对于棱柱形的对象——面板、平板、垫片，以及任何从等厚原材料上切出来的东西——每一个深度上的轮廓都是同一个。而对于截面在切削过程中会变化的对象，并不存在唯一正确的答案，于是加工路径以底面为准，并明确说明这一点：给出一条警告，指出两端相差多少。因为由用户没有料到的轮廓生成出来的路径，正是那种一路到机床上都看起来像成功了的失败。此外也没有引入线、没有连接片、没有斜向下刀——刀具在每条轮廓的起点直接扎刀，而在最后一刀走完时零件就自由了。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:942
msgid "``pc convert``"
msgstr "``pc convert``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:943
msgid ""
"Convert parts, sketches, assemblies or scenes to another format and update "
"their type in the package. Subcommands: ``part``, ``sketch``, ``assembly`` "
"and ``scene``. An assembly converts between ``assy`` and ``urdf``: to URDF "
"it writes the ``.urdf`` file and the meshes it references; to ASSY it writes"
" an ``stl`` part for every URDF link, an interface pair for every joint, and"
" an ``.assy`` that places the parts with ``connect:``. A scene converts "
"between ``assy`` and any file format the package graph reads as a scene -- "
"``sim-gazebo:world`` and ``sim-mujoco:mjcf`` are the two today, each from "
"its engine's plugin package. To such a format it writes the file and the "
"meshes it references; to ASSY it copies every shape the file places into the"
" package as a part of its own and writes an ``.assy`` that places them. "
"Which formats those are is not a fixed list -- it is whatever the graph "
"declares under ``import:`` with ``scene`` among its ``kinds`` -- so a "
"package that teaches PartCAD an arrangement format converts to and from it "
"too."
msgstr ""
"把零件、草图、装配体或场景转换成另一种格式，并更新它们在包中的类型。子命令： ``part`` 、 ``sketch`` 、 ``assembly`` "
"和 ``scene`` 。装配体可以在 ``assy`` 与 ``urdf`` 之间转换：转为 URDF 时，它会写出 ``.urdf`` "
"文件以及它所引用的网格；转为 ASSY 时，它会为每个 URDF 连杆写出一个 ``stl`` 零件，为每个关节写出一对接口，并写出一个用 "
"``connect:`` 放置这些零件的 ``.assy`` 。场景可以在 ``assy`` 与包依赖图能够作为场景读取的任何文件格式之间转换——今天有"
" ``sim-gazebo:world`` 和 ``sim-mujoco:mjcf`` "
"两种，各自来自相应引擎的插件包。转为这类格式时，它会写出该文件以及它所引用的网格；转为 ASSY "
"时，它会把该文件所放置的每一个形状都复制进包中作为包自己的零件，并写出一个放置它们的 ``.assy`` "
"。具体有哪些格式并不是一份固定的清单——凡是依赖图在 ``import:`` 下声明、且 ``kinds`` 中含有 ``scene`` "
"的都算——因此，一个教会 PartCAD 认识某种布置格式的包，也就同时支持与该格式之间的互转。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:954
msgid "``pc filter``"
msgstr "``pc filter``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:955
msgid ""
"Declare a second assembly (or scene) made of some of the links of an "
"existing one::"
msgstr "声明第二个装配体（或场景），它由某个已有装配体的部分链接组成： ::"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:959
msgid ""
"``FILTER`` names the links to keep -- a JSON or YAML file, or the same "
"written out on the command line -- and ``DST`` is the new object: the ASSY "
"file of ``SRC`` with everything the filter drops taken out of it, written as"
" ``DST.assy`` and declared beside ``SRC``. If ``SRC`` is an assembly then "
"``DST`` is an assembly, and if ``SRC`` is a scene then ``DST`` is a scene; "
"``-a``/``-S`` say which, without looking it up. An existing ``DST`` is "
"overwritten, and ``--dry-run`` says what would be written without writing "
"it."
msgstr ""
"``FILTER`` 指名要保留哪些链接 -- 可以是一个 JSON 或 YAML 文件，也可以把同样的内容直接写在命令行上 -- 而 ``DST`` "
"是新的对象：它就是 ``SRC`` 的 ASSY 文件去掉过滤器所丢弃的全部内容之后的结果，写作 ``DST.assy`` 并声明在 ``SRC`` "
"旁边。如果 ``SRC`` 是装配体，``DST`` 就是装配体；如果 ``SRC`` 是场景，``DST`` 就是场景；``-a``/``-S`` "
"可以直接说明是哪一种，从而省掉查找。已存在的 ``DST`` 会被覆盖，而 ``--dry-run`` 只说明会写出什么而不真正写出。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:971
msgid ""
"What a filter is, and what naming a link with and without children means, is"
" the same everywhere it is accepted -- see :ref:`assy-filter`, which also "
"covers the ``--filter`` of the two commands below and the equivalent in the "
"VS Code viewer. The short of it: a link the filter names is kept, a link it "
"does not name is dropped, and a link named with children under it keeps "
"those children only."
msgstr ""
"过滤器是什么，以及指定一个链接时带不带其子链接各是什么含义，在所有接受过滤器的地方都是一样的——参见 :ref:`assy-filter` "
"，那里也涵盖了下面两条命令的 ``--filter`` 以及 VS Code "
"查看器中的等价功能。简而言之：过滤器指定的链接会被保留，没有指定的链接会被丢弃，而指定时带上了子链接的链接则只保留那些子链接。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:976
msgid ""
"The **file** is filtered rather than the built assembly, so every link kept "
"keeps its ``connect:``, its ``how:``, its parameters and its comments, and "
"the result is an assembly somebody can build. That needs an Assembly YAML "
"file to work from: an assembly held in a foreign format has no links of its "
"own, and ``pc convert assembly -t assy`` is what turns one into a file that "
"does."
msgstr ""
"被过滤的是 **文件** 而不是已构建的装配体，因此每一个保留下来的链接都会保留它的 ``connect:`` 、 ``how:`` "
"、参数和注释，得到的结果是一个别人可以真正构建出来的装配体。这需要有一个 Assembly YAML "
"文件作为出发点：以外来格式保存的装配体没有自己的链接，而 ``pc convert assembly -t assy`` "
"正是把它变成一个有链接的文件的办法。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:981
msgid ""
"Dropping a link that another link was connected to is the one thing "
"filtering can break, and it is checked: every ``connect:`` left pointing at "
"nothing is reported, naming the line, by this command and by ``pc lint`` "
"afterwards."
msgstr ""
"丢掉一个本来被其他链接连接着的链接，是过滤唯一可能破坏的东西，而这一点是会被检查的：每一条指向空处的 ``connect:`` "
"都会被报告并指明所在行，本命令会报告，之后的 ``pc lint`` 也会报告。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:985
msgid "``pc export``"
msgstr "``pc export``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:986
msgid ""
"Export a 3D view of parts, assemblies, or scenes. The object is found by its"
" name whatever its kind (see :ref:`object-names`). Choose the format with "
"``-t``: ``step``, ``brep``, ``stl``, ``3mf``, ``threejs``, ``obj``, "
"``gltf``, ``iges``, ``urdf``, or any file type a package implements itself "
"(see :ref:`output-files`). Use ``-O`` to set the output directory, and ``-P "
"<package>...`` or ``...:<name>`` to export the packages below this one too "
"(see :ref:`recursive-names`). ``urdf`` writes a ``.urdf`` file plus a "
"directory of the mesh files it references."
msgstr ""
"导出零件、装配体或场景的 3D 视图。对象不论是哪种类型都按它的名称找到（参见 :ref:`object-names` ）。使用 ``-t`` "
"选择格式：``step``、``brep``、``stl``、``3mf``、``threejs``、``obj``、``gltf``、``iges``、``urdf``，或者某个包自行实现的任意文件类型（参见"
" :ref:`output-files` ）。使用 ``-O`` 设置输出目录，使用 ``-P <package>...`` 或 "
"``...:<name>`` 可一并导出其下层的包（参见 :ref:`recursive-names` ）。``urdf`` 会写出一个 "
"``.urdf`` 文件，外加一个存放它所引用的网格文件的目录。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:994
msgid ""
"``--filter`` exports a *part* of one assembly or scene: the links it names, "
"where the assembly put them, without writing anything into the package (see "
":ref:`assy-filter`). It applies to one named assembly or scene, so it is "
"refused for a part, for a whole package and for a ``...`` subtree. A "
"``filter:`` on an ``export:`` file type asks for the same thing permanently,"
" per file type, and this overrides it for one run."
msgstr ""
"``--filter`` 导出一个装配体或场景的 *一部分*：它所指名的那些链接，位置就是装配体给它们安排的位置，并且不会向包中写入任何内容（参见 "
":ref:`assy-filter` ）。它只适用于一个具名的装配体或场景，所以对零件、对整个包以及对 ``...`` "
"子树都会被拒绝。``export:`` 文件类型上的 ``filter:`` 是在按文件类型永久性地提出同样的要求，而这个选项会为单次运行覆盖它。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1000
msgid ""
"``-t`` also takes a full path, ``-t sim-gazebo:world``, which names the "
"package the implementation lives in. That is how a format PartCAD ships no "
"implementation of is reached, and an engine's own scene format is exactly "
"that: a Gazebo world (SDFormat) is written by `partcad-sim-gazebo "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad-sim-gazebo>`_ and a MuJoCo model (MJCF) "
"by `partcad-sim-mujoco <https://github.com/partcad/partcad-sim-mujoco>`_, "
"beside the reader and the simulator that share their knowledge of the "
"format, so ``-t sim-gazebo:world`` is the spelling that resolves and a bare "
"``-t world`` resolves to nothing. Both write a file plus a directory of the "
"meshes it references, the way ``urdf`` does. ``-e`` names a further package "
"whose ``export:`` options and implementations are used, which is how one "
"package's exporter is applied to another package's objects -- the same "
"answer for every file type at once, where ``-t <package>:<type>`` is the "
"answer for one."
msgstr ""
"``-t`` 也接受完整路径，如 ``-t sim-gazebo:world`` ，它指明了实现所在的包。PartCAD "
"没有自带实现的格式正是这样被用到的，而引擎自有的场景格式就属于这一类：Gazebo 世界（SDFormat）由 `partcad-sim-gazebo "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad-sim-gazebo>`_ 写出，MuJoCo 模型（MJCF）由 "
"`partcad-sim-mujoco <https://github.com/partcad/partcad-sim-mujoco>`_ "
"写出，与同样掌握该格式知识的读取器和仿真器放在一起，因此 ``-t sim-gazebo:world`` 才是能解析成功的写法，而单写 ``-t "
"world`` 什么也解析不到。两者都会像 ``urdf`` 那样写出一个文件外加一个存放其所引用网格的目录。 ``-e`` 指定另一个包，使用它的 "
"``export:`` 选项和实现，这样就能把一个包的导出器应用到另一个包的对象上——它一次性为所有文件类型给出同一个答案，而 ``-t "
"<package>:<type>`` 只为某一种文件类型给出答案。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1012
msgid "``pc render``"
msgstr "``pc render``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1013
msgid ""
"Render a 2D projection of parts, assemblies, or scenes onto a plane. Choose "
"the format with ``-t``: ``svg``, ``png``, ``jpeg``, ``dxf``, ``readme``, "
"``pdf``, ``html``, or any file type a package implements itself (see "
":ref:`output-files`). ``-e`` works the same way as it does for ``pc "
"export``, reading the ``render:`` options from another package. ``-P "
"<package>...`` and ``...:<name>`` render a whole subtree, the same way they "
"do for ``pc export`` (see :ref:`recursive-names`). ``-p <name>=<value>`` "
"renders the object with that value of one of its parameters, the same as "
"naming it ``<name>;<parameter>=<value>`` (see :ref:`parameter-values`)."
msgstr ""
"把零件、装配体或场景的 2D 投影渲染到一个平面上。使用 ``-t`` "
"选择格式：``svg``、``png``、``jpeg``、``dxf``、``readme``、``pdf``、``html``，或者某个包自行实现的任意文件类型（参见"
" :ref:`output-files` ）。``-e`` 的用法与它在 ``pc export`` 中相同，即从另一个包读取 ``render:`` "
"选项。``-P <package>...`` 和 ``...:<name>`` 可渲染整个子树，用法与它们在 ``pc export`` 中相同（参见 "
":ref:`recursive-names` ）。``-p <name>=<value>`` 以对象某个参数的该取值来渲染它，与把它指名为 "
"``<name>;<parameter>=<value>`` 等效（参见 :ref:`parameter-values` ）。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1021
msgid ""
"``--filter`` renders a *part* of one assembly or scene, exactly as it does "
"for ``pc export`` above:"
msgstr "``--filter`` 渲染一个装配体或场景的 *一部分* ，用法与它在上面的 ``pc export`` 中完全相同："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1028
msgid ""
"The file it writes is the one an unfiltered render would have written, under"
" the object's own name, so two filters of one object overwrite each other --"
" use ``-O`` to send them to directories of their own. Unlike ``pc filter``, "
"this leaves the package untouched and can select inside a link that places "
"another package's assembly, because what is filtered is the assembly that "
"was built rather than any file."
msgstr ""
"它写出的文件，就是一次不带过滤的渲染本会写出的那个文件，使用对象自己的名字，因此对同一个对象用两个过滤器会互相覆盖——请用 ``-O`` "
"把它们分别送进各自的目录。与 ``pc filter`` "
"不同，这条命令完全不改动包，并且可以在一个放置了其他包装配体的链接内部进行选择，因为被过滤的是已经构建出来的装配体，而不是任何文件。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1033
msgid ""
"A ``filter:`` on a ``render:`` file type says the same thing permanently and"
" **per file type**, so one object can have a picture of one sub-assembly "
"checked in beside the drawing of the whole of it. It is read in either place"
" a file type is configured -- the package's ``render:`` section and the "
"object's own -- and ``--filter`` overrides it for one run, the way "
"``--view`` overrides a configured viewport. See :ref:`assy-filter`."
msgstr ""
"``render:`` 文件类型上的 ``filter:`` 是在 **按文件类型** "
"永久性地提出同样的要求，因此同一个对象可以把某个子装配体的图片与整体的工程图一起提交进版本库。配置文件类型的两个地方——包的 ``render:`` "
"小节和对象自己的小节——都会读取它，而 ``--filter`` 会为单次运行覆盖它，就像 ``--view`` 覆盖已配置的视口那样。参见 "
":ref:`assy-filter` 。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1039
msgid ""
"``--port`` draws one named port rather than every one of them, and is "
"repeated for several. A port is named the way the log names it -- its own "
"name for a port of the object, and the path of links then the port for one "
"inside an assembly, ``head/head_half_1`` becoming ``head:head_half_1:TL-m3``"
" -- which is also the path the VS Code viewer shows as rows. It says *which*"
" ports rather than that any are drawn, so it goes with one of the three "
"options below:"
msgstr ""
"``--port`` "
"只绘制指定名称的那一个端口，而不是全部端口；要绘制多个就重复给出该选项。端口的命名方式与日志中的一致——对象自身的端口用它自己的名字，而装配体内部的端口则用链接路径加端口名，例如"
" ``head/head_half_1`` 写作 ``head:head_half_1:TL-m3`` ——这也正是 VS Code "
"查看器以行的形式显示的那个路径。它说明的是绘制 *哪些* 端口，而不是要不要绘制端口，因此需要与下面三个选项之一一起使用："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1049
msgid ""
"``--with-ports`` draws every port of the object on the projection: a "
"coordinate frame at each, with the long arrow along ``+Z`` — the direction a"
" part travels along when it is connected through that port — and the name a "
"``connectPorts:`` would have to use, joined to it by a line. ``--with-"
"interfaces`` names each *instance* of an interface once, draws a line from "
"that name out to each port that belongs to it, and draws each port's "
"boundary sketch where the port is. ``--with-all`` draws both. Every port "
"drawn is also listed in the log, with the exact name to write in an Assembly"
" YAML file."
msgstr ""
"``--with-ports`` 会在投影上绘制该对象的每一个端口：每个端口处画一个坐标系，其中长箭头沿 ``+Z`` "
"——也就是零件通过该端口连接时所沿着的方向——并以一条引线连到 ``connectPorts:`` 中必须使用的那个名字上。 ``--with-"
"interfaces`` 则为接口的每一个 *实例* 各标注一次名称，从该名称向属于它的每一个端口各画一条引线，并在端口所在处画出该端口的边界草图。 "
"``--with-all`` 两者都画。每一个被绘制的端口也会在日志中列出，并给出在 Assembly YAML 文件中应当书写的确切名称。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1056
msgid ""
"The names are written around the object rather than on it: spread evenly "
"around it, each on the side its port is on, and with its line made as long "
"as it takes for no name to land on the object or on another name."
msgstr ""
"这些名称写在对象周围而不是写在对象上：均匀地分布在它四周，各自位于其端口所在的那一侧，并且引线会被拉到足够长，以保证没有任何名称落在对象上或落在另一个名称上。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1059
msgid ""
"An assembly is taken at its word: what is drawn is what it says its ports "
"are -- the ones its ``map:`` externalizes and the ones it declares (see "
":ref:`assembly-ports`) -- and not everything inside it. That is the same "
"boundary ``pc info`` and a ``connect:`` see, and an assembly that "
"externalizes three ports of the forty it contains means those three. "
"``--with-internals`` draws what is inside one anyway, each child's ports "
"placed where the assembly put the child, which is how a connection that went"
" wrong is found: two frames that should have met and did not. On its own it "
"asks for nothing; it says how deep the three options above reach."
msgstr ""
"装配体的说法会被照单全收：绘制出来的是它所声称的那些端口——由它的 ``map:`` 对外暴露的，以及它自己声明的（参见 :ref:`assembly-"
"ports` ）——而不是它内部的一切。这与 ``pc info`` 和 ``connect:`` "
"所看到的边界是同一个，一个把它所包含的四十个端口中的三个对外暴露的装配体，指的就是那三个。 ``--with-internals`` "
"则会把内部的内容也画出来，每个子对象的端口都画在装配体安置该子对象的位置上，出错的连接正是这样被找出来的：两个本该相遇却没有相遇的坐标系。它本身不要求绘制任何东西；它说明的是上面三个选项要深入到哪一层。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1067
msgid ""
"The options apply to whichever format is being written — the projection is "
"the same one underneath ``svg``, ``png``, ``jpeg`` and ``dxf`` — and a "
"package can ask for the same thing permanently, by declaring "
"``with_ports:``, ``with_interfaces:`` or ``with_internals:`` on a file type "
"of its own (see :ref:`output-files`, and ``examples/feature_interface``, "
"which keeps four such drawings checked in). ``port_marker_size`` and "
"``port_label_size`` set how big the markers and the names are, as a fraction"
" of the projection's largest dimension."
msgstr ""
"这些选项适用于正在写出的任何一种格式——在 ``svg`` 、 ``png`` 、 ``jpeg`` 和 ``dxf`` "
"之下，投影本身是同一个——而包也可以在自己的某个文件类型上声明 ``with_ports:`` 、 ``with_interfaces:`` 或 "
"``with_internals:`` 来永久性地提出同样的要求（参见 :ref:`output-files` ，以及 "
"``examples/feature_interface`` ，那里有四张这样的图提交在版本库中）。 ``port_marker_size`` 和 "
"``port_label_size`` 设定标记和名称的大小，取值是投影最大尺寸的一个比例。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1075
msgid ""
"A port is a coordinate frame rather than geometry, but it is projected like "
"everything else: the axis it is offset along is the one a given projection "
"collapses, so two frames a millimetre apart along the line of sight are "
"drawn one on top of the other. A port that comes out ambiguous is worth the "
"same second and third ``--view`` below that an ambiguous feature is."
msgstr ""
"端口是一个坐标系而不是几何体，但它和其他一切一样会被投影：它所沿着偏移的那根轴，正是某个投影所压缩掉的那根轴，因此沿视线方向相距一毫米的两个坐标系会被画成上下重叠的样子。出现歧义的端口，和出现歧义的特征一样，值得用下面所说的第二个、第三个"
" ``--view`` 再看一遍。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1080
msgid ""
"``--view`` picks the direction the object is looked at from for this one "
"run: ``front``, ``back``, ``left``, ``right``, ``top``, ``bottom`` or "
"``iso``. Each name is shorthand for a pair of vectors, which ``--viewport-"
"origin`` and ``--viewport-up`` give as ``X,Y,Z`` instead: the first is the "
"direction the object is looked at from (``0,-100,0`` is the front of any "
"object, wherever it sits), the second is which way is up in the resulting "
"picture. Either one replaces the vector the name resolved to, so ``--view "
"top --viewport-up 0,1,0.5`` tilts the top view without spelling the rest of "
"it out:"
msgstr ""
"``--view`` "
"为这一次运行选择观察对象的方向：``front``、``back``、``left``、``right``、``top``、``bottom`` 或 "
"``iso``。每个名字都是一对向量的简写，而 ``--viewport-origin`` 和 ``--viewport-up`` 则以 "
"``X,Y,Z`` 的形式直接给出这对向量：前者是观察对象的方向（ ``0,-100,0`` "
"就是任何对象的正面，不管它摆在哪里），后者是最终画面中哪个方向朝上。两者中的任何一个都会替换掉名字所解析出的那个向量，因此 ``--view top "
"--viewport-up 0,1,0.5`` 可以在不把其余部分全部写出来的情况下，把俯视图倾斜一点："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1093
msgid ""
"All three are the ``viewport_origin`` and ``viewport_up`` of a render file "
"type in ``partcad.yaml`` (see :ref:`output-files`), passed for one command "
"instead of written down — so they layer on top of whatever the package and "
"the object configured, and a file type that does not project (``step``, "
"``readme``, an assembly instruction book) never reads them. PartCAD is Z-up "
"with ``+Y`` pointing away from the front view, which is what puts ``+X`` on "
"the right of it."
msgstr ""
"这三者就是 ``partcad.yaml`` 中某个渲染文件类型的 ``viewport_origin`` 和 ``viewport_up`` （参见 "
":ref:`output-files` ），只不过是为单条命令传入而不是写进配置——因此它们会叠加在包和对象已有的配置之上，而不做投影的文件类型（ "
"``step`` 、 ``readme`` 、装配说明书）则从不读取它们。PartCAD 采用 Z 轴朝上， ``+Y`` "
"指向远离主视图的方向，这也正是 ``+X`` 位于主视图右侧的原因。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1099
msgid ""
"A rendered file is named after the object, so several views of one object go"
" into directories of their own rather than over each other:"
msgstr "渲染出的文件以对象命名，因此同一个对象的多个视图要分别放进各自的目录，否则会互相覆盖："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1109
msgid ""
"``-t readme`` generates a markdown document instead of a projection: the "
"package document (``README.md``, listing what the package declares) or, when"
" the object named is an assembly, that assembly's own document "
"(``<assembly>.md``, listing the bill of materials — every part and sub-"
"assembly it is made of, recursively, grouped by the package they come from "
"and counted). An assembly can also ask for its own document in the package "
"configuration, by declaring ``readme`` in its ``render`` section."
msgstr ""
"``-t readme`` 生成的是一份 markdown 文档而不是投影：可以是包的文档（ ``README.md`` "
"，列出该包所声明的内容），也可以在所指名的对象是一个装配体时，生成该装配体自己的文档（ ``<assembly>.md`` ，列出物料清单 — "
"它由哪些零件和子装配体递归构成，按它们所来自的包分组并计数）。装配体也可以在包配置中通过在它的 ``render`` 小节里声明 ``readme`` "
"来索取自己的文档。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1115
msgid ""
"Only assemblies that a package declares are listed as sub-assemblies. An "
"assembly embedded in an Assembly YAML file's nested ``links:`` section "
"belongs to no package, so it is not listed on its own: the parts it holds "
"are counted towards the assembly that embeds it."
msgstr ""
"只有包所声明的装配体才会作为子装配体列出。嵌在 Assembly YAML 文件的嵌套 ``links:`` "
"小节中的装配体不属于任何包，因此不会被单独列出：它所包含的零件会计入嵌入它的那个装配体。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1119
msgid ""
"``-t pdf`` and ``-t html`` generate the assembly instruction book of the "
"assembly named: a title page, the same bill of materials, then a page per "
"assembly step, in the order the Assembly YAML file lists the links. Whatever"
" has to be made before a step can be done is explained just before it: a "
"sub-assembly gets a page showing it as it should look once it is together, "
"followed by its own steps, and a part that is manufactured rather than "
"bought gets a page saying what it is made from, its manufacturing "
"instructions written out, and — where it declares a job a route can be "
"produced for (see ``pc cam``) — the route drawn from above. Something used "
"in several places is explained once, with how many to make, in the lowest-"
"level assembly that holds every place it is used, so it is made before the "
"first step that needs it. ``pc render`` writes the complete book — every "
"sub-assembly that is built and every part that is — and ``pc instructions`` "
"below writes as much of it as is asked for."
msgstr ""
"``-t pdf`` 和 ``-t html`` 生成所指名装配体的装配说明书：一个标题页、同样的物料清单，然后按 Assembly YAML "
"文件列出链接的顺序，每个装配步骤一页。每一步能够进行之前必须先做好的东西，都会紧挨着这一步加以说明：子装配体会有一页展示它装好之后应有的样子，随后是它自己的各个步骤；而需要制造而不是购买的零件会有一页说明它由什么制成、把它的制造说明写出来，并且在它声明了可以生成加工路径的作业时（参见"
" ``pc cam`` "
"），附上自上方绘制的加工路径。在多处用到的东西只说明一次，并注明要做多少个，位置放在包含它全部使用位置的那个最底层装配体中，这样它会在第一个需要它的步骤之前被做出来。``pc"
" render`` 写出的是完整的说明书 -- 每一个需要构建的子装配体和每一个需要制造的零件都在内 -- 而下文的 ``pc "
"instructions`` 则按要求写出其中的一部分。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1130
msgid ""
"A step is what a person does at once: one item put in place, and the "
"fasteners that hold it. A link whose joint is made by going into the "
"material — a screw cutting its own thread, a pin snapped in (``selfScrew``, "
"``snapIn``) — and that is connected to the item of the step before it, or "
"driven through it (``interferes``), is driven in at that step rather than at"
" a step of its own. A step page shows:"
msgstr ""
"一个步骤就是一个人一次性完成的事：把一个项目放到位，再加上固定它的那些紧固件。如果某条链接的接合是靠进入材料实现的 — "
"自攻螺钉自己切出螺纹、被按进去的销钉（ ``selfScrew``、``snapIn`` ）— 而它又连接到上一个步骤的那个项目上，或者被压过那个项目（"
" ``interferes`` ），那么它就在那一步里被装进去，而不是单独占一个步骤。步骤页会展示："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1135
msgid ""
"the parts to pick out, in a box with how many of each: every fastener, and "
"the item itself when it is under a quarter of the size of the finished "
"assembly. A board or a panel is what the pictures are of; a screw is too "
"small to find in them, and is counted here;"
msgstr ""
"要挑出来的零件，装在一个方框里并标明每种要几个：所有紧固件，以及当该项目本身小于成品装配体尺寸四分之一时也包括它。图片画的是一块板或一块面板；螺钉在图里小到找不到，所以在这里计数；"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1138
msgid ""
"the item going on: everything placed before the step in grey — the assembly "
"so far, which is what the reader has in front of them — and the item in "
"blue, held off the joint, with a line drawn across the gap it opens. That "
"gap is half of the largest dimension of the item and what it is joined to, "
"unless the step sets ``exploded:`` in its ``connect:`` or ``connectPorts:`` "
"section (see :doc:`/assy`);"
msgstr ""
"正在装上去的那个项目：这一步之前已经放置好的一切用灰色表示 — 也就是目前为止的装配体，读者手上拿着的就是它 — "
"而该项目用蓝色表示，悬在接合处之外，并在它张开的那个间隙上画一条连线。这个间隙是该项目与它所接合对象两者最大尺寸的一半，除非该步骤在它的 "
"``connect:`` 或 ``connectPorts:`` 小节中设置了 ``exploded:`` （参见 :doc:`/assy` ）；"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1142
msgid ""
"when it is fastened, beside it, the fasteners going in: only the parts they "
"join, in place, and the fasteners pulled out of their holes along the line "
"they go in by;"
msgstr "当它需要被紧固时，在它旁边画出正在装入的紧固件：只画它们所接合的那些零件，摆在原位，而紧固件则沿着它们装入的方向从各自的孔里拉出来；"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1144
msgid ""
"the words of the ASSY file — the node's ``description`` — and below them, "
"smaller, the model's account of the joint: which ports of what meet, how it "
"goes on, the further joints the item makes (``alsoConnectPorts``), and how "
"many fasteners go into what, through what."
msgstr ""
"ASSY 文件里的文字 — 也就是该节点的 ``description`` — "
"以及在它下面、字号更小的、模型对这个接合处的说明：什么东西的哪些端口相遇、它是怎么装上去的、该项目还形成了哪些接合（ "
"``alsoConnectPorts`` ），以及有多少个紧固件、装进什么、穿过什么。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1148
msgid ""
"Every step of an assembly is drawn from the one iso view that most of what "
"moves in it comes out towards, so that one picture follows on from the one "
"before; the fastening of a step is drawn from the side its fasteners are "
"driven from. The last page collects links: to this assembly and its package,"
" to every other package that supplies at least three of its parts, and to "
"PartCAD. The HTML is one self-contained file that shows a single page at a "
"time, with arrows on either side (and the arrow keys) to flip through it. As"
" with ``readme``, an assembly can ask for either document in the package "
"configuration, by declaring ``pdf`` or ``html`` in its ``render`` section."
msgstr ""
"装配体的每一个步骤都从同一个等轴视角绘制，也就是这一步中大多数运动的东西朝之而来的那个方向，这样一张图片就能接着上一张往下看；而某一步的紧固过程是从它的紧固件被拧入的那一侧绘制的。最后一页汇总各种链接：指向本装配体及其所属的包、指向每一个至少提供了它三个零件的其他包，以及指向"
" PartCAD。HTML 是一个自包含的文件，一次显示一页，两侧有箭头（也可以用方向键）来翻页。与 ``readme`` "
"一样，装配体也可以在包配置中通过在它的 ``render`` 小节里声明 ``pdf`` 或 ``html`` 来索取这两种文档。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1156
msgid ""
"Declaring one with a ``path`` says the opposite: that this ``pdf`` is a file"
" of the package's own — a drawing, a datasheet — written by that "
"implementation like any other file type, and no instruction book is "
"generated over it (see :ref:`output-files`)."
msgstr ""
"而带 ``path`` 来声明它则表示相反的意思：这个 ``pdf`` "
"是包自己的一个文件——一张工程图、一份数据手册——像其他任何文件类型一样由相应实现写出，并且不会再在它之上生成装配说明书（参见 "
":ref:`output-files` ）。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1160
msgid ""
"Both formats are only defined for an assembly declared as ``type: assy``: "
"the steps come from the Assembly YAML file, and an assembly that has none is"
" refused rather than reduced to a title page and a parts list. An assembly "
"that is not meant to be built at all (``manufacturable: false``, on the "
"assembly or inherited from its package) is refused too; pass ``--ignore-"
"manufacturability`` to generate the document anyway."
msgstr ""
"这两种格式都只对声明为 ``type: assy`` 的装配体有定义：步骤来自 Assembly YAML "
"文件，而没有步骤的装配体会被拒绝，而不是被简化成一个标题页加一份零件清单。完全不打算被制造的装配体（在装配体上声明、或从它所属的包继承而来的 "
"``manufacturable: false`` ）同样会被拒绝；要无论如何都生成该文档，请传入 ``--ignore-"
"manufacturability`` 。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1165
msgid "``pc instructions``"
msgstr "``pc instructions``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1166
msgid ""
"Write the assembly instructions of the assembly named, as ``-t pdf`` (the "
"default) or ``-t html``, into the current directory or the one ``-O`` names."
" It is the book ``pc render -t pdf`` writes, and the one the IDE's "
"**Assembly** tab shows and saves; what differs is that it asks how much of "
"it to write:"
msgstr ""
"把所指定装配体的装配说明写入当前目录或 ``-O`` 所指定的目录，格式为 ``-t pdf`` （默认）或 ``-t html`` 。它就是 ``pc"
" render -t pdf`` 写出的那本说明书，也是 IDE 的 **Assembly** "
"选项卡所显示并保存的那一本；区别在于它可以指定要写出其中的多少内容："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1170
msgid ""
"on its own, this assembly's own steps, in the order of its links, with a "
"sub-assembly added as the finished thing it is;"
msgstr "单独使用时，写出本装配体自己的各个步骤，顺序与它的链接一致，其中子装配体按它装好后的成品形态加入；"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1172
msgid ""
"``-r``/``--recursive`` puts in the steps of every sub-assembly that is "
"built, each just before the step that adds it;"
msgstr "``-r`` / ``--recursive`` 会把每一个需要构建的子装配体的步骤也放进来，各自紧挨在添加它的那一步之前；"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1174
msgid ""
"``-b``/``--build-parts`` puts in how to make every part that is built, each "
"just before the step that first needs it. Primitive for now: the "
"manufacturing instructions written out, and the route drawn where a part "
"declares one."
msgstr ""
"``-b`` / ``--build-parts`` "
"会把每一个需要制造的零件的做法也放进来，各自紧挨在第一个需要它的步骤之前。目前还比较简陋：写出制造说明，并在零件声明了加工路径时把路径画出来。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1178
msgid ""
"What is built and what is bought is what was chosen in the IDE's **Build vs "
"Buy** tab for this assembly, which keeps the choices on the machine they "
"were made on, in ``~/.partcad/garage/default/bvb/<assembly, escaped>.json``."
" Where nothing was chosen, a line item that can be either is bought, as the "
"bill of materials assumes. The steps and pages come in the very order the "
"IDE's **Build** tab lists them in, so a step selected there and a page of "
"the file are the same step."
msgstr ""
"哪些东西是自己做、哪些是买来的，取决于在 IDE 的 **Build vs Buy** "
"选项卡中为该装配体所做的选择，这些选择保存在做出选择的那台机器上，位于 "
"``~/.partcad/garage/default/bvb/<assembly, escaped>.json`` "
"。凡是没有做出选择的，两者皆可的条目一律按购买处理，这与物料清单的假设一致。步骤和页面的顺序与 IDE 的 **Build** "
"选项卡所列出的顺序完全一致，因此在那里选中的某一步与文件中的某一页就是同一步。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1184
msgid ""
"The file is written by ``pc`` itself, on the machine it runs on, whichever "
"machine the daemon is on."
msgstr "该文件由 ``pc`` 自己写出，写在它自己运行的那台机器上，无论守护进程在哪台机器上。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1193
msgid "Interacting with IDE"
msgstr "与 IDE 交互"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1195
msgid ""
"Putting an object in front of a person, in one of two windows -- the IDE's "
"own **Digital Thread** (``pc ide view``), or **another application** on this"
" machine (``pc ide open``, which is also what the editor extension's \"Open "
"in...\" menu runs) -- and asking the IDE what it is showing (``pc ide "
"state``). Two more set the IDE up: ``pc ide install`` puts the PartCAD "
"extension into an editor, and ``pc ide workspace <directory>`` opens a "
"package as an editor's workspace, in the PartCAD workbench. None of them "
"leaves anything new in the package: that is what ``pc export`` and ``pc "
"render`` are for. ``pc ide view`` and ``pc ide open`` used to be ``pc "
"inspect`` and ``pc open``; those names still work, are left out of ``pc "
"--help``, and print a note on stderr saying what to type instead."
msgstr ""
"把一个对象呈现在人面前，可以在两种窗口之一中进行 -- IDE 自带的 **Digital Thread** （ ``pc ide view`` "
"），或者本机上的 **另一个应用程序** （ ``pc ide open`` ，编辑器扩展的“Open in...”菜单运行的也是它）-- 还可以询问 "
"IDE 当前在显示什么（ ``pc ide state`` ）。另外两条命令用来配置 IDE：``pc ide install`` 把 PartCAD "
"扩展装进某个编辑器，而 ``pc ide workspace <directory>`` 把一个包作为编辑器的工作区打开，并进入 PartCAD "
"工作台。它们都不会在包里留下任何新东西：那是 ``pc export`` 和 ``pc render`` 的事。``pc ide view`` 和 "
"``pc ide open`` 以前叫 ``pc inspect`` 和 ``pc open`` ；那些名称仍然可用，不会出现在 ``pc "
"--help`` 中，并会在 stderr 上提示改用什么。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1204
msgid "``pc ide view``"
msgstr "``pc ide view``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1205
msgid ""
"View a part, assembly, or scene in the Digital Thread. Use ``-V`` for a "
"verbal (text) description instead of a visual one, and ``-p <name>=<value>``"
" to set parameters."
msgstr ""
"在 Digital Thread 中查看零件、装配体或场景。使用 ``-V`` 获取文字描述而不是可视化显示，使用 ``-p "
"<name>=<value>`` 设置参数。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1208
msgid ""
"One flag per tab of the viewer opens it on that tab, named "
"``--<group>-<tab>`` the way the viewer's two strips read: ``--design-3d``, "
"``--design-2d``, ``--design-draft``; ``--analysis-fea``, ``--analysis-"
"dynamic``, ``--analysis-thermal``, ``--analysis-cfd``; ``--manufacturing-"
"bvb``, ``--manufacturing-build``, ``--manufacturing-buy``, "
"``--manufacturing-bom``, ``--manufacturing-assembly``; ``--validation-"
"test``, ``--validation-simulation``. With none, the viewer stays on "
"whichever tab it is on. The analysis tabs and the Simulation tab list what "
"the object declares -- its scenarios of that analysis, its simulations -- "
"and select the first; ``--scenario <name>`` selects the one of that name "
"instead, and is refused with any other tab. The tab travels with the shape, "
"so it is the window that draws the object that switches; a tab that does not"
" apply to the object (FEA of an assembly) is not opened, and one that is not"
" known yet (Build, until the viewer has worked out what is built; "
"Simulation, until it has read what the object declares under ``simulate:``) "
"is opened as soon as it is. Opening an analysis tab runs the scenario it "
"selects, and opening Simulation runs the simulation it selects, as clicking "
"them does."
msgstr ""
"查看器的每一个标签页都有一个标志用来直接在那个标签页上打开它，命名为 ``--<group>-<tab>`` "
"，读法与查看器的两条标签条一致：``--design-3d``、``--design-2d``、``--design-draft`` "
"；``--analysis-fea``、``--analysis-dynamic``、``--analysis-"
"thermal``、``--analysis-cfd`` ；``--manufacturing-bvb``、``--manufacturing-"
"build``、``--manufacturing-buy``、``--manufacturing-bom``、``--manufacturing-"
"assembly`` ；``--validation-test``、``--validation-"
"simulation``。一个都不给时，查看器停留在它当前所在的标签页上。各个分析标签页和 Simulation 标签页会列出该对象所声明的内容 -- "
"它那项分析的各个场景、它的各个仿真 -- 并选中第一个；``--scenario <name>`` "
"则改为选中那个名称的一项，而与任何其他标签页同时使用都会被拒绝。标签页是跟着形状走的，所以切换的是绘制该对象的那个窗口；不适用于该对象的标签页（比如装配体的"
" FEA）不会被打开，而一个尚未确定的标签页（Build，在查看器算出什么是自制的之前；Simulation，在它读到该对象 ``simulate:``"
" 下所声明的内容之前）会在一确定之后立刻打开。打开一个分析标签页会运行它所选中的那个场景，打开 Simulation "
"会运行它所选中的那个仿真，与点击它们的效果相同。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1227
msgid "``pc ide install``"
msgstr "``pc ide install``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1228
msgid ""
"Install the PartCAD extension into an editor on this machine -- the PartCAD "
"IDE, VSCodium or Visual Studio Code, whichever of ``partcad-ide``, "
"``codium`` and ``code`` is found first on the ``PATH``, or the one "
"``--with`` names (by name or path). The package is the "
"``partcad-<version>.vsix`` published on PartCAD's GitHub release -- the "
"latest one, or the one ``--version`` names -- or a ``.vsix`` on disk given "
"with ``--vsix``. Anything after ``--`` goes on the editor's command line, "
"which is how a profile of its own is used:"
msgstr ""
"把 PartCAD 扩展安装到本机的某个编辑器里 -- PartCAD IDE、VSCodium 或 Visual Studio Code，取 "
"``partcad-ide``、``codium`` 和 ``code`` 中在 ``PATH`` 上最先找到的那一个，或者取 ``--with`` "
"所指名的那一个（按名称或路径）。安装包是 PartCAD GitHub 发布页上发布的 ``partcad-<version>.vsix`` -- "
"最新的那一个，或者 ``--version`` 所指名的那一个 -- 也可以是用 ``--vsix`` 给出的、磁盘上的某个 "
"``.vsix``。``--`` 之后的内容都会附到编辑器的命令行上，这也是使用它自己的配置档的办法："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1241
msgid ""
"``PARTCAD_BASE_URL`` replaces the release's download directory, as it does "
"for ``pc upgrade``. Like ``pc upgrade``, it changes this machine and asks no"
" daemon anything."
msgstr ""
"``PARTCAD_BASE_URL`` 替换发布版的下载目录，与它对 ``pc upgrade`` 的作用相同。与 ``pc upgrade`` "
"一样，它改变的是本机，并且不向任何守护进程询问任何事情。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1244
msgid "``pc ide workspace``"
msgstr "``pc ide workspace``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1245
msgid ""
"Open a directory -- by default the current one -- as the workspace of an "
"editor on this machine, in the **PartCAD workbench**: the window comes up on"
" the PartCAD Explorer rather than on the files. The editor is found the way "
"``pc ide install`` finds one, or named with ``--with``, and anything after "
"``--`` goes on its command line."
msgstr ""
"把一个目录 -- 默认是当前目录 -- 作为本机某个编辑器的工作区打开，并进入 **PartCAD 工作台**：窗口打开时呈现的是 PartCAD "
"Explorer，而不是文件列表。编辑器的查找方式与 ``pc ide install`` 相同，也可以用 ``--with`` 指名，而 ``--``"
" 之后的内容都会附到它的命令行上。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1256
msgid ""
"An editor's command line can open a folder but not run a command in the "
"window it opens, so ``pc ide workspace`` leaves a request under "
"``~/.partcad/ide/requests/`` first, and the PartCAD extension takes it as it"
" starts in that folder's window, or as an existing window of that folder "
"comes to the front. A request nobody takes is ignored after five minutes. "
"The extension starts in a folder that holds PartCAD files (a "
"``partcad.yaml``, an ASSY file, a script); any other folder is opened "
"without the workbench. It is not ``pc ide open``, which puts one object in "
"front of a person in a design application and waits for it to come back "
"edited; this returns as soon as the editor has the folder."
msgstr ""
"编辑器的命令行可以打开一个文件夹，却无法在它打开的那个窗口里运行命令，所以 ``pc ide workspace`` 会先在 "
"``~/.partcad/ide/requests/`` 下留下一个请求，而 PartCAD "
"扩展会在那个文件夹的窗口中启动时、或者在该文件夹已有的窗口被切到前台时把它取走。五分钟内没人取走的请求会被忽略。扩展只在装有 PartCAD "
"文件的文件夹中启动（一个 ``partcad.yaml`` 、一个 ASSY 文件、一个脚本）；其他任何文件夹都会被打开，但不进入工作台。它不是 "
"``pc ide open`` -- "
"后者把一个对象呈现在人面前的某个设计应用程序里，并等着它被编辑完回来；而这条命令在编辑器拿到该文件夹之后就立即返回。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1264
msgid "``pc ide state``"
msgstr "``pc ide state``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1265
msgid ""
"Print what the PartCAD IDE on this machine is showing, as YAML (the default)"
" or ``--json``::"
msgstr "打印本机上的 PartCAD IDE 当前显示的内容，格式为 YAML（默认）或 ``--json``::"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1270
msgid "One document, one entry per view:"
msgstr "一份文档，每个视图一项："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1272
msgid ""
"``explorer`` -- what is selected in the PartCAD Explorer: each row's "
"``kind`` (``part``, ``assembly``, ``package``, ...), its full ``path`` "
"(``//pub/examples:cube``, or a package's own path), what it is declared as "
"and the file it is read from."
msgstr ""
"``explorer`` ——PartCAD Explorer 中选中的内容：每一行的 ``kind`` "
"（``part``、``assembly``、``package`` 等）、完整的 ``path`` "
"（``//pub/examples:cube``，或者包自身的路径）、它被声明成什么，以及它从哪个文件读取。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1275
msgid ""
"``inspector`` -- the object the PartCAD Inspector shows: its properties, "
"every parameter it declares with what the field holds **now** (``value``), "
"and what the object was last shown with (``applied``). The two differ when a"
" value has been typed and Update not pressed. ``live: false`` says the "
"Inspector's panel could not be asked -- it is collapsed -- and the values "
"are the applied ones."
msgstr ""
"``inspector`` ——PartCAD Inspector "
"显示的对象：它的属性，它声明的每一个参数，以及该字段**当前**的内容（``value``）和对象上次显示时使用的值（``applied``）。如果输入了值却没有按"
" Update，两者就会不同。``live: false`` 表示无法询问 Inspector 面板（它被折叠了），此时报告的是已应用的值。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1279
msgid ""
"``viewer`` -- the Digital Thread: the ``tab`` and ``subTab`` on screen "
"(``design``/``2d``), what every tab strip offers and which tabs are "
"disabled, and for **each sub-tab** its ``filters`` -- what it would send "
"``pc render --filter``, or ``null`` for the whole object -- and its "
"``selections``: the boxes ticked in its tree, the port overlays on the 2D "
"tab, and the value of every control in its pane (format, drawing package, "
"switches). They differ by sub-tab, which is why each has its own entry. "
"``screenshot`` is the path of a PNG of the sub-tab on screen, written by the"
" IDE into its temporary directory (``/tmp/partcad-viewer-"
"design-2d-<time>.png`` on Linux); when one cannot be taken -- the panel is "
"closed, or hidden behind another editor -- ``screenshotError`` says why."
msgstr ""
"``viewer`` ——Digital Thread：屏幕上的 ``tab`` 和 ``subTab`` "
"（``design``/``2d``），每个标签栏提供哪些标签、哪些被禁用，以及**每个子标签**的 ``filters`` ——它会发给 ``pc "
"render --filter`` 的内容，整个对象则为 ``null`` ——和它的 ``selections`` ：它的树中勾选的方框、2D "
"标签上的端口叠加层，以及它面板中每个控件的值（格式、绘图包、开关）。这些因子标签而异，所以每个子标签各有一项。``screenshot`` "
"是屏幕上那个子标签的 PNG 路径，由 IDE 写入它的临时目录（在 Linux 上是 ``/tmp/partcad-viewer-"
"design-2d-<time>.png``）；无法截图时——面板已关闭，或被另一个编辑器挡住——由 ``screenshotError`` 说明原因。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1288
msgid ""
"The IDE is asked over the socket ``pc ide view`` shows things on, so this "
"needs no daemon and no workspace, and runs where the IDE does. The 3D view's"
" text callouts are drawn over the canvas rather than in it, so they are not "
"in its screenshot. With two VS Code windows open on Linux, the kernel hands "
"the question to one of them; ``window.workspaceFolders`` says which one "
"answered."
msgstr ""
"询问 IDE 用的是 ``pc ide view`` 显示内容的同一个套接字，因此不需要守护进程，也不需要工作区，在 IDE 所在的地方运行即可。3D "
"视图的文字标注是叠加在画布之上而不是画在画布里的，所以截图中没有它们。在 Linux 上打开两个 VS Code "
"窗口时，内核会把询问交给其中一个；``window.workspaceFolders`` 会说明是哪一个回答的。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1293
msgid "``pc ide open``"
msgstr "``pc ide open``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1294
msgid "Open a file in a third-party application, on this machine::"
msgstr "在这台机器上用第三方应用程序打开一个文件： ::"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1304
msgid ""
"``--with`` names the application: ``freecad`` (the default), ``blender`` and"
" ``kicad`` for a board are the ones PartCAD itself ships. ``gazebo`` and "
"``mujoco`` come from the plugin package for that engine (`partcad-sim-gazebo"
" <https://github.com/partcad/partcad-sim-gazebo>`_, `partcad-sim-mujoco "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad-sim-mujoco>`_), beside the reader, the "
"exporter and the simulator for its scene format, so they are offered in a "
"workspace that imports one and are an unknown application anywhere else. A "
"locally installed one is always used when there is one: the command looks on"
" the ``PATH``, in ``/Applications`` on macOS, under ``Program Files`` on "
"Windows, and for a flatpak on Linux. Gazebo is looked for under all three of"
" the names it has had (``gz sim``, ``ign gazebo``, ``gazebo``), and "
"whichever the machine has is the one used."
msgstr ""
"``--with`` 指定应用程序： ``freecad`` （默认）、 ``blender`` ，以及用于电路板的 ``kicad`` ，这几个是 "
"PartCAD 自己提供的。 ``gazebo`` 和 ``mujoco`` 来自相应引擎的插件包（ `partcad-sim-gazebo "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad-sim-gazebo>`_ 、 `partcad-sim-mujoco "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad-sim-mujoco>`_ "
"），与该引擎场景格式的读取器、导出器和仿真器放在一起，因此它们只在导入了相应插件包的工作区中可用，在其他任何地方都是未知的应用程序。只要本机装有该应用程序，就一定会使用本机的：命令会在"
" ``PATH`` 上查找，在 macOS 上查找 ``/Applications`` ，在 Windows 上查找 ``Program Files``"
" ，在 Linux 上还会查找 flatpak。Gazebo 会按它用过的全部三个名字（ ``gz sim`` 、 ``ign gazebo`` 、 "
"``gazebo`` ）查找，机器上有哪个就用哪个。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1314
msgid ""
"**``pc ide open`` waits for the application to close**, and then brings back"
" what was done in it. Each application declares what it opens, best first "
"(``formats:`` in its ``open:`` entry -- FreeCAD's is ``fcstd``, ``step``, "
"``brep``, ``iges``, ``stl``, ``obj``; Blender's is ``blend`` and the meshes "
"it imports). A file already in one of them is opened as it is. Any other is "
"converted to the first one PartCAD can write, and the application is given "
"that: a STEP file, a CadQuery script or a 3MF mesh reaches Blender as STL, "
"and a build123d script reaches FreeCAD as STEP. Converting is the one thing "
"``pc ide open`` asks the PartCAD daemon for, because turning a solid into a "
"mesh is CAD work; the window still opens on the machine the command was run "
"on. The converted copy is written under this workspace's own directory "
"(never beside your file), named after the object it came from, and reused "
"until that object changes. ``--type`` says what the file holds when its name"
" does not -- a ``.py`` is a CadQuery script, a build123d one or an SDF one "
"-- and the VS Code extension passes the declared type of the object you "
"clicked."
msgstr ""
"**``pc ide open`` 会等待应用程序关闭**，然后把在其中所做的修改带回来。每个应用程序都声明自己能打开什么，最佳的排在前面（其 "
"``open:`` 条目中的 ``formats:`` ——FreeCAD 的是 "
"``fcstd``、``step``、``brep``、``iges``、``stl``、``obj``；Blender 的是 ``blend`` "
"以及它能导入的网格格式）。已经是其中某种格式的文件按原样打开。其他文件会转换为 PartCAD 能写出的第一种格式，再交给应用程序：STEP "
"文件、CadQuery 脚本或 3MF 网格以 STL 的形式交给 Blender，build123d 脚本以 STEP 的形式交给 "
"FreeCAD。转换是 ``pc ide open`` 唯一要请 PartCAD 守护进程做的事，因为把实体变成网格属于 CAD "
"工作；窗口仍然在运行命令的那台机器上打开。转换后的副本写在这个工作区自己的目录下（绝不会放在你的文件旁边），以其来源对象命名，在该对象发生变化之前一直重复使用。文件名无法说明内容时，用"
" ``--type`` 指明——``.py`` 可能是 CadQuery 脚本、build123d 脚本或 SDF 脚本——VS Code "
"扩展会传入所点击对象的声明类型。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1326
msgid ""
"``--kind sketch`` says the file holds a sketch, which is converted between "
"sketch formats rather than part formats: an application that opens drawings "
"-- CADCraft, from the ``partcad-cadcraft`` plugin, lists DWG and DXF -- is "
"handed a DXF sketch as it is, and an SVG sketch or a CadQuery or build123d "
"one as the DXF PartCAD draws of it::"
msgstr ""
"``--kind sketch`` 说明该文件装的是一张草图，于是它是在各草图格式之间转换，而不是在零件格式之间转换：对于打开图纸的应用程序 -- "
"比如来自 ``partcad-cadcraft`` 插件的 CADCraft，它列出 DWG 和 DXF -- DXF 草图原样交过去，而 SVG "
"草图、CadQuery 或 build123d 草图则交给它 PartCAD 为其绘制的那个 DXF::"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1333
msgid ""
"The type alone does not say which: a ``cadquery`` file declared under "
"``sketches:`` is a drawing, the same file under ``parts:`` a solid. The VS "
"Code extension passes the kind of the object you clicked."
msgstr ""
"单凭类型说明不了是哪一种：在 ``sketches:`` 下声明的 ``cadquery`` 文件是一张图纸，而同一个文件在 ``parts:`` "
"下就是一个实体。VS Code 扩展会把你所点击对象的类型传过去。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1336
msgid ""
"When the application closes, the file it was given is compared with what it "
"was before:"
msgstr "应用程序关闭时，会把交给它的文件与之前的状态进行比较："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1338
msgid "**Unchanged** -- nothing happens, and ``No changes.`` says so."
msgstr "**未改动**——什么也不做，并以 ``No changes.`` 说明。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1339
msgid "**Changed, and opened as it is** -- the edit is already in your file."
msgstr "**已改动，且是按原样打开的**——修改已经在你的文件里了。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1340
msgid ""
"**Changed, and converted first** -- the edited copy is converted back into "
"the object's own format and written over its source, when that source is a "
"file PartCAD can write (``step``, ``brep``, ``stl``, ``3mf``, ``obj``, "
"``iges``, ``gltf``; for a sketch, ``dxf`` and ``svg``). A script is not: its"
" edit is kept where it was made and the path is printed, because overwriting"
" the program that generates a part with its output would destroy the "
"program."
msgstr ""
"**已改动，且之前做过转换** -- 当对象的来源是 PartCAD 能写出的文件时（ "
"``step``、``brep``、``stl``、``3mf``、``obj``、``iges``、``gltf`` ；对草图而言是 ``dxf`` "
"和 ``svg`` "
"），编辑后的副本会被转换回对象自己的格式并覆盖其来源。脚本不在此列：它的修改留在原处，并打印出路径，因为用生成零件的程序的输出去覆盖这个程序，会把程序毁掉。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1346
msgid ""
"An application that saves beside what it opened -- KiCad -- has its whole "
"directory compared rather than the one file. Interrupting ``pc ide open`` "
"(``Ctrl+C``) stops the wait and leaves the application open; what is saved "
"in it from then on is not brought back."
msgstr ""
"对于把内容保存在所打开文件旁边的应用程序——KiCad——比较的是整个目录，而不是那一个文件。中断 ``pc ide open`` "
"（``Ctrl+C``）会结束等待，并让应用程序继续开着；此后在其中保存的内容不会被带回。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1350
msgid ""
"MuJoCo reads MJCF and no other model format, and a scene that is not already"
" one is **not** converted here. That is not an omission: MJCF is written by "
"``partcad-sim-mujoco``'s exporter and a Gazebo world is read by ``partcad-"
"sim-gazebo``'s reader, and a file handed to ``pc ide open`` has no package "
"around it to reach either through. So such a file is refused with the export"
" that does work rather than converted wrongly. An application's ``open:`` "
"entry names the extensions its own format is stored in "
"(``sceneExtensions``), which is how a file that already is one goes straight"
" over without any conversion at all."
msgstr ""
"MuJoCo 只读取 MJCF，不读取任何其他模型格式，而本来就不是 MJCF 的场景在这里 **不会** 被转换。这并非疏漏：MJCF 由 "
"``partcad-sim-mujoco`` 的导出器写出，Gazebo 世界由 ``partcad-sim-gazebo`` 的读取器读取，而交给 "
"``pc ide open`` "
"的文件外面没有包，无法借由包去使用其中任何一个。因此这样的文件会被拒绝，并提示那条确实可行的导出路径，而不是被错误地转换。应用程序的 ``open:``"
" 条目列出了它自己的格式所使用的扩展名（ ``sceneExtensions`` ），正因如此，本来就是该格式的文件可以完全不经转换直接交过去。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1357
msgid ""
"An object that only means something inside a package -- an ASSY file, a URDF"
" -- has nothing to convert ad-hoc, and is refused with that for the same "
"reason: export it to a mesh first (``pc export -t stl``), or a scene to its "
"engine's format (``pc export -t sim-mujoco:mjcf``), and open that."
msgstr ""
"只有在包内部才有意义的对象 -- ASSY 文件、URDF -- 没有可以即时转换的东西，出于同样的原因也会被拒绝：请先把它导出为网格（ ``pc "
"export -t stl`` ），或者把场景导出为其引擎的格式（ ``pc export -t sim-mujoco:mjcf`` "
"），再打开导出的结果。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1361
msgid ""
"KiCad is handed the board rather than the file named, when the two are not "
"the same: a ``kicad`` part *is* the STEP file KiCad's command line writes "
"out of the board, so ``pc ide open --with kicad`` on it opens the "
"``.kicad_pro`` (or ``.kicad_pcb``, or ``.kicad_sch``) beside it. Nothing is "
"created here and nothing is rendered -- a file with no board beside it is "
"handed over as it is. Every application but Blender is given the file it was"
" pointed at, whatever it holds."
msgstr ""
"当电路板与所指定的文件不是同一个东西时，交给 KiCad 的是电路板而不是那个文件： ``kicad`` 零件本身 *就是* KiCad "
"命令行从电路板写出的 STEP 文件，因此对它执行 ``pc ide open --with kicad`` 打开的是旁边的 "
"``.kicad_pro`` （或 ``.kicad_pcb`` 、 ``.kicad_sch`` "
"）。这里不会创建任何东西，也不会渲染任何东西——旁边没有电路板的文件会按原样交过去。除 Blender "
"之外的每一个应用程序，拿到的都是它被指向的那个文件，无论里面装的是什么。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1367
msgid ""
"With ``--use-docker``, a machine that has no local installation runs the "
"application in a container instead, started the way PartCAD starts every "
"container (see :ref:`useDockerRemote <use-docker-remote>`): named ``partcad-"
"open-<application>-<tag>-<identity>``, labelled so that ``pc system prune`` "
"removes it, replaced rather than reused when what it was created from has "
"changed, and running PartCAD's own container service, through which the "
"application is launched. The image is the one the application's ``open:`` "
"entry declares under ``container:`` (``--docker-image`` overrides it): "
"FreeCAD's is ``linuxserver/freecad:latest``, since the FreeCAD project "
"publishes no image of its own, Blender's is ``linuxserver/blender:latest`` "
"for the same reason, KiCad's is the ``ghcr.io/partcad/partcad-container-"
"kicad`` image PartCAD already builds for ``kicad`` parts, and an engine's is"
" whatever its plugin package declares. The application's own settings live "
"in a volume of their own (``partcad-open-<application>-home``), so they "
"outlast the container. Without ``--use-docker``, a machine with neither the "
"application nor Docker is told so rather than being left with a command that"
" quietly did nothing."
msgstr ""
"使用 ``--use-docker`` 时，没有本地安装的机器会改在容器中运行应用程序，容器的启动方式与 PartCAD 启动任何容器相同（参见 "
":ref:`useDockerRemote <use-docker-remote>`）：命名为 ``partcad-"
"open-<application>-<tag>-<identity>``，带有标签以便 ``pc system prune`` "
"删除它，当创建它所依据的内容发生变化时会被替换而不是重用，并运行 PartCAD 自己的容器服务，应用程序通过该服务启动。镜像是应用程序的 "
"``open:`` 条目在 ``container:`` 下声明的那个（``--docker-image`` 可覆盖）：FreeCAD 用 "
"``linuxserver/freecad:latest``，因为 FreeCAD 项目没有发布自己的镜像；Blender 出于同样的原因用 "
"``linuxserver/blender:latest``；KiCad 用 PartCAD 本来就为 ``kicad`` 零件构建的 "
"``ghcr.io/partcad/partcad-container-kicad`` "
"镜像；仿真引擎则用其插件包声明的镜像。应用程序自己的设置保存在单独的卷中（``partcad-"
"open-<application>-home``），因此比容器存在得更久。不使用 ``--use-docker`` 时，既没有该应用程序也没有 "
"Docker 的机器会得到明确提示，而不是留下一条悄无声息什么也没做的命令。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1380
msgid ""
"The file reaches the container one of two ways, and ``useDockerRemote`` "
"chooses:"
msgstr "文件以两种方式之一进入容器，由 ``useDockerRemote`` 选择："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1382
msgid ""
"**mount** (the default) -- the directory holding the file is mounted at the "
"path it has on the host, so one path means the same thing on both sides, and"
" the application saves straight into it. In a dev container holding the "
"host's Docker socket, each directory is bound from where the host's daemon "
"keeps it -- the workspace's bind, ``/tmp``'s volume -- at the path it has in"
" the dev container, which is how the ``docker`` Python sandbox binds them "
"too. A file on none of the dev container's mounts is refused with the ways "
"out (mount it, ``PC_DOCKER_MOUNT_SOURCES``, or ``useDockerRemote``). Outside"
" any workspace, only the file's own directory is mounted -- not the "
"directory the command was run from."
msgstr ""
"**mount** （默认）——把包含该文件的目录以它在主机上的路径挂载进去，这样同一个路径在两边含义相同，应用程序直接保存到其中。在持有主机 "
"Docker 套接字的开发容器里，每个目录都从主机守护进程保存它的位置绑定——工作区的绑定挂载、``/tmp`` "
"的卷——并挂载到它在开发容器中的路径上，``docker`` Python "
"沙箱也是这样绑定的。不在开发容器任何挂载上的文件会被拒绝，并给出解决办法（挂载它、设置 ``PC_DOCKER_MOUNT_SOURCES``，或使用 "
"``useDockerRemote``）。不在任何工作区内时，只挂载文件自己所在的目录，而不是运行命令时所在的目录。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1389
msgid ""
"**upload** (``useDockerRemote: true``, or ``PC_USE_DOCKER_REMOTE=true``) -- "
"nothing is mounted. The file (or, for KiCad, its directory) is sent with the"
" request that launches the application, and what it is when the application "
"closes is sent back and written here. This is what a Docker daemon on "
"another machine needs. A ``fileArgs`` template that quotes the path inside a"
" script (``{path_repr}``) cannot be sent this way and is refused; "
"``{path}``, the path as an argument of its own, can."
msgstr ""
"**upload** （``useDockerRemote: true``，或 "
"``PC_USE_DOCKER_REMOTE=true``）——不挂载任何东西。文件（对 KiCad "
"而言是其目录）随启动应用程序的请求一起发送，应用程序关闭时它的状态再被发送回来并写到这里。另一台机器上的 Docker "
"守护进程需要的就是这种方式。把路径加引号嵌入脚本中的 ``fileArgs`` 模板（``{path_repr}``）无法以这种方式发送，会被拒绝；而 "
"``{path}`` （作为独立参数的路径）可以。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1395
msgid ""
"A containerised application draws on the host's X display. On Linux that "
"display is usually a socket, which is shared with the container along with "
"its authority cookie, and nothing needs configuring; a display reached over "
"TCP — a forwarded one, or an X server on macOS or Windows (XQuartz, VcXsrv) "
"— has to be installed and allowed to accept the connection. When there is "
"none, the command says which one to install and what to run rather than "
"starting a container whose window never appears."
msgstr ""
"容器化的应用程序使用宿主机的 X 显示。在 Linux 上该显示通常是一个套接字，它会连同其授权 cookie 一起共享给容器，无需任何配置；而通过 "
"TCP 访问的显示——转发来的显示，或 macOS、Windows 上的 X "
"服务器（XQuartz、VcXsrv）——则必须先安装好，并允许它接受连接。如果一个都没有，命令会告诉你该安装哪一个、该运行什么，而不是启动一个窗口永远不会出现的容器。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1401
msgid ""
"Like ``pc lint --file`` and ``pc upgrade``, this never talks to the daemon —"
" a daemon can be remote, where the window would open on somebody else's "
"screen. That is also why it takes a path rather than a ``<package>:<part>`` "
"name: resolving a name is a package-graph question, which is the round trip "
"this command does not make. ``--json`` prints what happened (or the reason "
"it did not) as one object, which is what the VS Code extension's \"Open "
"in...\" context menu reads."
msgstr ""
"与 ``pc lint --file`` 和 ``pc upgrade`` "
"一样，这条命令从不与守护进程通信——守护进程可能在远端，那样窗口就会打开在别人的屏幕上。这同时也是它接受路径而不是 "
"``<package>:<part>`` 名称的原因：解析名称是一个包依赖图的问题，而这条命令不会做那次往返。 ``--json`` "
"会把发生了什么（或者没能打开的原因）作为一个对象打印出来，VS Code 扩展的“Open in...”右键菜单读取的正是它。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1409
msgid "Interacting with AI agents"
msgstr "与 AI 智能体交互"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1411
msgid "``pc mcp``"
msgstr "``pc mcp``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1412
msgid ""
"Serve the `Model Context Protocol <https://modelcontextprotocol.io>`_ on "
"stdio, so that an AI agent can drive PartCAD: list a package's objects, read"
" their declarations, look at them (a render comes back as an image), test "
"them, export them, and run any other daemon method. An MCP client starts it "
"as a subprocess; it is a client of the workspace's daemon like every other "
"``pc`` command, and serves the package ``-p`` names, or the current "
"directory."
msgstr ""
"在 stdio 上提供 `Model Context Protocol <https://modelcontextprotocol.io>`_ 服务，让"
" AI 智能体可以驱动 "
"PartCAD：列出一个包的对象、读取它们的声明、查看它们（渲染结果以图片形式返回）、测试它们、导出它们，以及运行任何其他守护进程方法。MCP "
"客户端会把它作为子进程启动；它和其他每一条 ``pc`` 命令一样，都是本工作区守护进程的客户端，并为 ``-p`` 所指名的包、或者当前目录提供服务。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1423
msgid ""
"The agent may name files only inside the workspace unless ``--allow-path "
"DIR`` (repeatable) or ``--allow-any-path`` says otherwise. "
":doc:`/ai_agents/mcp` lists the tools and how each MCP client is set up."
msgstr ""
"除非 ``--allow-path DIR`` （可重复）或 ``--allow-any-path`` "
"另有说明，智能体只能指名工作区内部的文件。:doc:`/ai_agents/mcp` 列出了各个工具以及每种 MCP 客户端的配置方法。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1428
msgid "Workflow commands"
msgstr "工作流命令"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1430
msgid "``pc supply``"
msgstr "``pc supply``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1431
msgid "Manage the supply chain of the current project:"
msgstr "管理当前项目的供应链："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1433
msgid "``pc supply caps`` — Show the capabilities of a provider."
msgstr "``pc supply caps`` — 显示某个提供方的能力。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1434
msgid "``pc supply find`` — Find suppliers."
msgstr "``pc supply find`` — 查找供应商。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1435
msgid "``pc supply quote`` — Get a quote from suppliers."
msgstr "``pc supply quote`` — 从供应商处获取报价。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1436
msgid "``pc supply order`` — Place an order with suppliers."
msgstr "``pc supply order`` — 向供应商下订单。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1438
msgid ""
"``find`` and ``quote`` take parts and assemblies alike. A requested assembly"
" that is sold assembled (one with ``vendor`` and ``sku`` set, see "
":ref:`procurement`) is ordered as one item. Any other assembly is procured "
"as the objects it is made of, and the walk stops at every sub-assembly that "
"is sold assembled: such a sub-assembly is ordered as one item instead of "
"being taken apart. Pass ``--recursive`` (``-r``) to walk all the way down to"
" the parts regardless, and order those."
msgstr ""
"``find`` 和 ``quote`` 同样接受零件和装配体。所请求的装配体若是按整件出售的（即设置了 ``vendor`` 和 ``sku`` "
"，参见 :ref:`procurement` "
"），就按一个条目订购。其他任何装配体都会按它所由以构成的那些对象来采购，并且遍历会在每一个按整件出售的子装配体处停下：这样的子装配体会按一个条目订购，而不会被拆开。传入"
" ``--recursive`` （ ``-r`` ）可以无视这一点，一路遍历到零件，并按零件订购。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1446
msgid "Other commands"
msgstr "其他命令"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1448
msgid "``pc adhoc``"
msgstr "``pc adhoc``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1449
msgid ""
"Ad-hoc operations that run on the fly, on a file that belongs to no package:"
" PartCAD declares the file in a throwaway package of its own, produces one "
"output file, and deletes the package again. Nothing is created and nothing "
"is configured. Subcommands, each taking ``part`` or ``sketch``:"
msgstr ""
"即时执行的临时操作，作用于不属于任何包的文件：PartCAD "
"会把该文件声明在一个用完即弃的临时包中，产出一个输出文件，然后再把这个包删掉。不会创建任何东西，也不会配置任何东西。子命令如下，每一条都接受 "
"``part`` 或 ``sketch`` ："

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1453
msgid ""
"``pc adhoc convert`` — write the file back out as another format (``pc adhoc"
" convert part bracket.step bracket.stl``)."
msgstr ""
"``pc adhoc convert`` — 把该文件以另一种格式重新写出（ ``pc adhoc convert part bracket.step "
"bracket.stl`` ）。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1455
msgid ""
"``pc adhoc render`` — write a 2D projection of it: ``svg``, ``png``, "
"``jpeg`` or ``dxf`` (``pc adhoc render part --view top bracket.step "
"bracket.png``)."
msgstr ""
"``pc adhoc render`` — 写出它的一张 2D 投影： ``svg`` 、 ``png`` 、 ``jpeg`` 或 ``dxf`` （"
" ``pc adhoc render part --view top bracket.step bracket.png`` ）。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1458
msgid ""
"Both infer the types from the file names, and take ``--input``/``--output`` "
"to say them outright. ``pc adhoc render`` takes the same ``--view``, "
"``--viewport-origin`` and ``--viewport-up`` as ``pc render`` — and with no "
"``partcad.yaml`` to configure a viewport in, they are the only way to aim "
"one. The output file name may be left off when ``--output`` names the type: "
"the file is then named after the input."
msgstr ""
"两者都会根据文件名推断类型，也都接受 ``--input`` / ``--output`` 来直接指明类型。 ``pc adhoc render`` "
"接受与 ``pc render`` 相同的 ``--view`` 、 ``--viewport-origin`` 和 ``--viewport-up``"
" ——而且这里没有 ``partcad.yaml`` 可供配置视口，因此它们是瞄准视角的唯一办法。当 ``--output`` "
"已经指明了类型时，输出文件名可以省略：此时文件会以输入文件来命名。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1463
msgid ""
"Which of the two to use is which kind of file is wanted, and it is the same "
"distinction as between ``pc export`` and ``pc render``: geometry another CAD"
" tool can go on working with, or a picture. A file type a package implements"
" itself is available to neither, since there is no package here to declare "
"it in."
msgstr ""
"该用这两者中的哪一个，取决于想要哪一类文件，这与 ``pc export`` 和 ``pc render`` 之间的区别是一样的：是另一款 CAD "
"工具可以继续加工的几何，还是一张图片。包自行实现的文件类型对两者都不可用，因为这里没有包可供声明它。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1467
msgid ""
"The assembly formats ``assy`` and ``urdf`` are refused by both: an ASSY file"
" is a set of references to the parts of a package and a URDF becomes a part "
"per link, so neither means anything without one. Declare it in a package and"
" use ``pc convert assembly``, ``pc export`` or ``pc render`` instead."
msgstr ""
"装配体格式 ``assy`` 和 ``urdf`` 会被两者拒绝：ASSY 文件是一组指向某个包中零件的引用，而 URDF "
"的每个连杆都会变成一个零件，因此离开了包，两者都毫无意义。请把它声明在一个包中，改用 ``pc convert assembly`` 、 ``pc "
"export`` 或 ``pc render`` 。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1471
msgid "``pc healthcheck``"
msgstr "``pc healthcheck``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1472
msgid ""
"Check the host system for known issues. Use ``--dry-run`` to list the "
"available checks, ``--filters`` to run only checks with the given tags, and "
"``--fix`` to attempt automatic fixes."
msgstr ""
"检查主机系统是否存在已知问题。使用 ``--dry-run`` 列出可用的检查项，使用 ``--filters`` 仅运行带有指定标签的检查，使用 "
"``--fix`` 尝试自动修复。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1475
msgid ""
"One of them is about this repository rather than the host: ``AgentSkills`` "
"compares the AI agent skills installed here against the PartCAD running, and"
" reports the ones an older release wrote. ``pc upgrade`` replaces PartCAD "
"and leaves them where they are, so without this an agent goes on reading "
"instructions for a CLI that has moved -- silently, since a stale skill looks"
" exactly like a current one. ``--fix`` reinstalls them, for the agents that "
"had them and no others."
msgstr ""
"其中有一项检查针对的是本仓库而不是主机： ``AgentSkills`` 会把这里安装的 AI 智能体技能与正在运行的 PartCAD "
"作比较，并报告出那些由较旧发布版本写出的技能。 ``pc upgrade`` 会替换 "
"PartCAD，却把这些技能原地留下，因此如果没有这项检查，智能体就会继续照着一个早已变化的 CLI "
"的说明去做——而且是悄无声息地，因为过时的技能看起来和最新的一模一样。 ``--fix`` 会重新安装它们，只针对本来就装了技能的那些智能体。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1481
msgid "``pc search``"
msgstr "``pc search``"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1482
msgid ""
"Search for objects by keyword. Subcommands: ``all``, ``parts``, "
"``sketches``, ``assemblies``, ``scenes``, ``interfaces``, and ``packages``. "
"``-P`` names the package to search, the root package by default; ``-P "
"<package>...`` searches the packages below it too (see :ref:`recursive-"
"names`)."
msgstr ""
"按关键字搜索对象。子命令： ``all`` 、 ``parts`` 、 ``sketches`` 、 ``assemblies`` 、 "
"``scenes`` 、 ``interfaces`` 和 ``packages`` 。 ``-P`` 指定要搜索的包，默认为根包；写成 ``-P "
"<package>...`` 时会一并搜索其下层的包（参见 :ref:`recursive-names` ）。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1486
msgid ""
"``pc search parts`` and ``pc search assemblies`` also take "
"``-i``/``--interface``, which searches by what an object *connects by* "
"rather than by what its declaration says: ``pc search parts -i m4-thru`` "
"finds every part with a 4mm through hole, and finds the ones that implement "
"``m4-thru-3`` or any other interface derived from it, because a part with a "
"3mm-thick 4mm through hole is a part with a 4mm through hole. An abstract "
"interface is therefore the most useful thing to search by -- it is the name "
"a whole family is known by. A bare name is the interface this package "
"declares, and ``//package:name`` is any other."
msgstr ""
"``pc search parts`` 和 ``pc search assemblies`` 还接受 ``-i`` / ``--interface`` "
"，它按对象 *通过什么来连接* 搜索，而不是按它的声明内容搜索： ``pc search parts -i m4-thru`` 会找出每一个带 4mm "
"通孔的零件，也会找出那些实现了 ``m4-thru-3`` 或任何其他由它派生出的接口的零件，因为一个板厚 3mm 的 4mm 通孔零件本来就是一个带 "
"4mm 通孔的零件。因此，抽象接口是最适合用来搜索的东西——它正是整整一族接口共用的那个名字。只写名字指的是本包所声明的接口，而 "
"``//package:name`` 则可以指任何其他包中的接口。"

#: ../../source/cli.rst:1493
msgid ""
"The answer comes from the declarations -- ``implements:``, and an assembly's"
" ``map:`` -- so nothing is built and nothing is instantiated to produce it; "
"the interfaces named in those declarations are resolved once per package and"
" kept for the rest of the run. ``--keyword`` and ``--interface`` may be "
"given together, and then both have to hold."
msgstr ""
"答案来自各处声明—— ``implements:`` ，以及装配体的 ``map:`` "
"——因此为了得出它，不会构建任何东西，也不会实例化任何东西；这些声明中所指定的接口，每个包只解析一次，并在本次运行的其余过程中一直保留。 "
"``--keyword`` 和 ``--interface`` 可以同时给出，此时两个条件都必须满足。"

